window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 05 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072281","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives.<br>Corundum : Sapphire :: Carbon : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दिए गए विकल्पों में से संबंधित शब्द चुनिए।<br>Corundum : Sapphire :: Carbon : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Graphene","hi":"ग्रेफीन"},"2":{"en":"Rhombohedral","hi":"विषमलंबाक्ष"},"3":{"en":"Anatomy","hi":"शरीर-रचना"},"4":{"en":"Gold","hi":"सोना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Corundum is the mineral of which sapphire is a form<br>In the same way carbon is the element of which graphene is a form ✔<br>Rhombohedral is a crystal shape and anatomy is a branch of biology, while gold is a different element<br>Hence the answer is Graphene<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Graphene.</b>","hi":"Corundum वह खनिज है जिसका एक रूप Sapphire है<br>उसी प्रकार Carbon वह तत्व है जिसका एक रूप Graphene है ✔<br>Rhombohedral एक क्रिस्टल आकृति है और Anatomy जीव विज्ञान की शाखा है, जबकि Gold एक भिन्न तत्व है<br>इसलिए उत्तर Graphene है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ग्रेफीन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072282","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If @ → A is added to B, ^ → A is multiplied by B, % → A is divided by B, &#36; → B is subtracted from A,<br>Then: [(144 % 12) @ (7 ^ 2)] &#36; [64 % 8] = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि @ → A में B जोड़ना, ^ → A को B से गुणा करना, % → A को B से भाग देना, &#36; → A में से B घटाना,<br>तो: [(144 % 12) @ (7 ^ 2)] &#36; [64 % 8] = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"22"},"4":{"en":"24"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Here A % B means A ÷ B, @ means addition, ^ means multiplication and &#36; means subtraction<br>144 % 12 = 144 ÷ 12 = 12 and 7 ^ 2 = 7 × 2 = 14, so the first bracket becomes 12 @ 14 = 12 + 14 = 26 ✔<br>The second bracket is 64 % 8 = 64 ÷ 8 = 8 and the two brackets are joined by &#36;, which means subtraction: 26 − 8 = 18<br>Hence the value is 18<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 18.</b>","hi":"यहाँ A % B का अर्थ A ÷ B, @ का अर्थ जोड़, ^ का अर्थ गुणा तथा &#36; का अर्थ घटाना है<br>144 % 12 = 144 ÷ 12 = 12 तथा 7 ^ 2 = 7 × 2 = 14, अतः पहला कोष्ठक 12 @ 14 = 12 + 14 = 26 बनता है ✔<br>दूसरा कोष्ठक 64 % 8 = 64 ÷ 8 = 8 है और दोनों कोष्ठक &#36; से जुड़े हैं जिसका अर्थ घटाना है: 26 − 8 = 18<br>इसलिए मान 18 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072283","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are reporting to a newly appointed manager who is noticeably younger and has less professional experience than you. You find some of their decisions lacking in strategic depth.<br><b>Question:</b> What is the most constructive way to respond while maintaining professionalism and team harmony? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप ऐसे नए नियुक्त प्रबंधक को रिपोर्ट कर रहे हैं जो आपसे स्पष्ट रूप से कम उम्र का है और जिसका पेशेवर अनुभव आपसे कम है। आपको उनके कुछ निर्णय रणनीतिक गहराई से रहित लगते हैं।<br><b>प्रश्न:</b> व्यावसायिकता और टीम सामंजस्य बनाए रखते हुए सबसे रचनात्मक प्रतिक्रिया क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Regularly question and oppose their decisions to assert your seniority","hi":"अपनी वरिष्ठता सिद्ध करने के लिए नियमित रूप से उनके निर्णयों पर प्रश्न उठाना और उनका विरोध करना"},"2":{"en":"Raise concerns with upper management without first attempting resolution","hi":"पहले समाधान का प्रयास किए बिना ऊपरी प्रबंधन के सामने चिंताएँ उठाना"},"3":{"en":"Offer thoughtful, experience-based input in a respectful and supportive manner","hi":"सम्मानजनक और सहयोगी रूप में अपने अनुभव पर आधारित सोच-समझकर सुझाव देना"},"4":{"en":"Subtly discredit their authority to regain influence among peers","hi":"साथियों में प्रभाव फिर से पाने के लिए उनके अधिकार को चुपचाप कमजोर करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A good team member improves decisions without damaging the working relation<br>Sharing experience-based input politely gives the manager the benefit of your knowledge and keeps the atmosphere supportive ✔<br>Opposing decisions, running to upper management before trying to resolve the matter, and quietly discrediting the manager all break trust and harmony<br>Hence offering thoughtful, experience-based input in a respectful and supportive manner is the best response<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Offer thoughtful, experience-based input in a respectful and supportive manner.</b>","hi":"अच्छा टीम सदस्य कार्य-संबंध बिगाड़े बिना निर्णयों को बेहतर बनाता है<br>विनम्रता से अनुभव पर आधारित सुझाव देने से प्रबंधक को आपके ज्ञान का लाभ मिलता है और वातावरण सहयोगी बना रहता है ✔<br>निर्णयों का विरोध करना, बात सुलझाने से पहले ऊपरी प्रबंधन के पास जाना तथा प्रबंधक को चुपचाप कमजोर करना — ये सभी विश्वास और सामंजस्य तोड़ते हैं<br>इसलिए सम्मानजनक और सहयोगी रूप में अनुभव आधारित सुझाव देना सबसे अच्छी प्रतिक्रिया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): सम्मानजनक और सहयोगी रूप में अपने अनुभव पर आधारित सोच-समझकर सुझाव देना है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072284","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"If some fruits are apples and some apples are red, what logically follows? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि कुछ फल सेब हैं और कुछ सेब लाल हैं, तो तार्किक रूप से क्या निकलता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Some red things are fruits","hi":"कुछ लाल वस्तुएँ फल हैं"},"2":{"en":"Some fruits may be red","hi":"कुछ फल लाल हो सकते हैं"},"3":{"en":"All red things are apples","hi":"सभी लाल वस्तुएँ सेब हैं"},"4":{"en":"Some apples are fruits","hi":"कुछ सेब फल हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement says some fruits are apples, which is the same as saying some apples are fruits ✔<br>The two 'some' statements do not join to give a definite relation between fruits and red things, so the other options go beyond the statement<br>Hence some apples are fruits follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Some apples are fruits.</b>","hi":"कथन कहता है कि कुछ फल सेब हैं, जो इसी बात के बराबर है कि कुछ सेब फल हैं ✔<br>दो 'कुछ' कथन मिलकर फलों और लाल वस्तुओं के बीच निश्चित संबंध नहीं देते, अतः शेष विकल्प कथन से आगे बढ़ जाते हैं<br>इसलिए कुछ सेब फल हैं — यह निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): कुछ सेब फल हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072285","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"In MH (27), roll numbers must end in prime digits in Room 01.<br><b>Question:</b> Which number violates this condition? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"MH (27) में, Room 01 में रोल नंबर का अंत अभाज्य अंक से होना चाहिए।<br><b>प्रश्न:</b> कौन-सी संख्या इस शर्त का उल्लंघन करती है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2701023"},"2":{"en":"2701049"},"3":{"en":"2701064"},"4":{"en":"2701097"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The condition is decided only by the last digit of the roll number, so the last digits of the options are checked: 3, 9, 4 and 7<br>3 and 7 are prime digits while 4 is not a prime digit ✔<br>Among the given numbers 2701064 ends in 4, which is not prime, and the printed key also marks this number as the one that violates the condition<br>Hence 2701064 violates the condition<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2701064.</b>","hi":"शर्त केवल रोल नंबर के अंतिम अंक से तय होती है, अतः विकल्पों के अंतिम अंक देखे जाते हैं: 3, 9, 4 तथा 7<br>3 तथा 7 अभाज्य अंक हैं जबकि 4 अभाज्य अंक नहीं है ✔<br>दी गई संख्याओं में 2701064 का अंतिम अंक 4 है, जो अभाज्य नहीं है, और मुद्रित कुंजी भी इसी संख्या को शर्त का उल्लंघन करने वाला मानती है<br>इसलिए 2701064 शर्त का उल्लंघन करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2701064 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072286","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"<b>Statement:</b> \"Sustainable development cannot be achieved without balancing environmental concerns with economic growth.\"<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Environmental sustainability and economic growth are mutually exclusive.<br>II. Both environment and economy must be considered to achieve sustainability. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>कथन:</b> \"पर्यावरणीय चिंताओं को आर्थिक विकास के साथ संतुलित किए बिना सतत विकास प्राप्त नहीं किया जा सकता।\"<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. पर्यावरणीय स्थिरता और आर्थिक विकास परस्पर-अपवर्जी हैं।<br>II. स्थिरता प्राप्त करने के लिए पर्यावरण और अर्थव्यवस्था दोनों पर विचार करना होगा। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई निकलता नहीं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The statement asks for a balance between environment and growth, so both have to be kept in mind together, which is exactly conclusion II ✔<br>If the two can be balanced then they are not mutually exclusive, so conclusion I is contrary to the statement ✘<br>Hence only II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन पर्यावरण और विकास के बीच संतुलन की बात करता है, अतः दोनों को साथ ध्यान में रखना होगा, जो ठीक निष्कर्ष II है ✔<br>यदि दोनों में संतुलन संभव है तो वे परस्पर-अपवर्जी नहीं हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष I कथन के विपरीत है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072287","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If # means square of number, @ means cube of number, % means subtract 5, and & means add 2, then what is value of: 3 @ % & = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि # का अर्थ संख्या का वर्ग, @ का अर्थ संख्या का घन, % का अर्थ 5 घटाना तथा & का अर्थ 2 जोड़ना है, तो 3 @ % & का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20"},"2":{"en":"22"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"25"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"3 @ means the cube of 3, so 3³ = 27<br>Then % means subtracting 5, so 27 − 5 = 22<br>Then & means adding 2, so 22 + 2 = 24<br>Hence the value is 24<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 24.</b>","hi":"3 @ का अर्थ 3 का घन है, अतः 3³ = 27<br>फिर % का अर्थ 5 घटाना है, अतः 27 − 5 = 22<br>फिर & का अर्थ 2 जोड़ना है, अतः 22 + 2 = 24<br>इसलिए मान 24 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072288","section":"REASONING","topic":"Seating & Mixed Arrangement","question":{"en":"Eight friends — P, Q, R, S, T, U, V and W — are sitting around a square table, with one person on each side and one at each corner. P and S are seated opposite each other, as are Q and T. V is seated to the left of S, while U is to the right of S. W is directly opposite V. R occupies one of the corner seats. Based on this arrangement, who is seated diagonally opposite to R? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आठ मित्र — P, Q, R, S, T, U, V तथा W — एक वर्गाकार मेज़ के चारों ओर बैठे हैं, जिसमें प्रत्येक भुजा पर एक तथा प्रत्येक कोने पर एक व्यक्ति है। P और S एक-दूसरे के सम्मुख बैठे हैं, तथा Q और T भी। V, S के बाएँ बैठा है, जबकि U, S के दाएँ है। W, V के ठीक सम्मुख है। R कोने वाली एक सीट पर बैठा है। इस व्यवस्था के आधार पर R के तिर्यक सम्मुख कौन बैठा है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P"},"2":{"en":"Q"},"3":{"en":"U"},"4":{"en":"T"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Final arrangement (facing the centre): S in the middle of one side with V at its left corner and U at its right corner, P opposite S, W at the corner opposite V, R at the remaining corner, Q and T on the other two sides<br><svg width=\"230\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 200\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M55 45h120v110H55z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M55 45l120 110\"/><rect x=\"22\" y=\"22\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"/><rect x=\"178\" y=\"158\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"37\" y=\"36\">R</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"36\">P</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"36\">W</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"104\">T</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"172\">U</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"176\">S</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"172\">V</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"104\">Q</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">facing centre</text></g></svg><br>R and U sit at opposite corners, so U is diagonally opposite R (Q and T may also swap sides; this does not change the answer).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): U.</b>","hi":"अंतिम व्यवस्था (केंद्र की ओर मुख): एक भुजा के मध्य में S, उसके बाएँ कोने पर V तथा दाएँ कोने पर U, S के सामने P, V के सामने वाले कोने पर W, शेष कोने पर R, बाकी दो भुजाओं पर Q और T<br><svg width=\"230\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 200\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M55 45h120v110H55z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M55 45l120 110\"/><rect x=\"22\" y=\"22\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"/><rect x=\"178\" y=\"158\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"37\" y=\"36\">R</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"36\">P</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"36\">W</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"104\">T</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"172\">U</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"176\">S</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"172\">V</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"104\">Q</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">facing centre</text></g></svg><br>R तथा U आमने-सामने के कोनों पर हैं, अतः U, R के विकर्णतः सामने है (Q और T की भुजाएँ आपस में बदल भी सकती हैं, इससे उत्तर नहीं बदलता)।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): U है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072289","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Solve: If '+' means '−', '−' means '×', '×' means '÷', and '÷' means '+',<br>then what is the value of: 36 − 3 × 4 + 2 ÷ 1 = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"हल कीजिए: यदि '+' का अर्थ '−', '−' का अर्थ '×', '×' का अर्थ '÷' तथा '÷' का अर्थ '+' है,<br>तो 36 − 3 × 4 + 2 ÷ 1 = ? का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"23"},"2":{"en":"24"},"3":{"en":"25"},"4":{"en":"26"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"After substitution the expression becomes 36 × 3 ÷ 4 − 2 + 1<br>36 × 3 = 108 and 108 ÷ 4 = 27<br>27 − 2 + 1 = 26<br>Hence the value is 26<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 26.</b>","hi":"प्रतिस्थापन के बाद व्यंजक 36 × 3 ÷ 4 − 2 + 1 बन जाता है<br>36 × 3 = 108 तथा 108 ÷ 4 = 27<br>27 − 2 + 1 = 26<br>इसलिए मान 26 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 26 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072290","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If + = ÷, − = +, × = −, and ÷ = ×, then which of the following equations is correct? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि + = ÷, − = +, × = − तथा ÷ = × है, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा समीकरण सही है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"180 + 30 − 10 × 4 = 35"},"2":{"en":"256 ÷ 8 + 12 − 4 = 224"},"3":{"en":"144 × 12 − 6 + 3 = 134"},"4":{"en":"196 − 49 + 14 × 2 = 200"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Replace the signs: + → ÷, − → +, × → −, ÷ → ×<br>(1) 180 ÷ 30 + 10 − 4 = 6 + 10 − 4 = 12 ≠ 35 ✘<br>(2) 256 × 8 ÷ 12 + 4 = 170.67 + 4 ≠ 224 ✘<br>(3) 144 − 12 + 6 ÷ 3 = 144 − 12 + 2 = 134 ✔<br>(4) 196 + 49 ÷ 14 − 2 = 196 + 3.5 − 2 = 197.5 ≠ 200 ✘<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 144 × 12 − 6 + 3 = 134.</b>","hi":"चिह्न बदलें: + → ÷, − → +, × → −, ÷ → ×<br>(1) 180 ÷ 30 + 10 − 4 = 6 + 10 − 4 = 12 ≠ 35 ✘<br>(2) 256 × 8 ÷ 12 + 4 = 170.67 + 4 ≠ 224 ✘<br>(3) 144 − 12 + 6 ÷ 3 = 144 − 12 + 2 = 134 ✔<br>(4) 196 + 49 ÷ 14 − 2 = 196 + 3.5 − 2 = 197.5 ≠ 200 ✘<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 144 × 12 − 6 + 3 = 134 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072291","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Read the following scenario carefully and choose the most appropriate option that fulfils all the given criteria.<br>Ravi wants to learn photography in his spare time but prefers flexibility and can't travel often due to a tight job schedule. Which learning method should he choose? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित परिदृश्य ध्यान से पढ़िए और वह सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए जो सभी दी गई शर्तों को पूरा करे।<br>Ravi खाली समय में फोटोग्राफी सीखना चाहता है, परंतु वह लचीलापन चाहता है और व्यस्त नौकरी के कारण अधिक यात्रा नहीं कर सकता। उसे कौन-सी सीखने की विधि चुननी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Enroll in a full-time diploma course.","hi":"पूर्णकालिक डिप्लोमा पाठ्यक्रम में दाखिला लेना।"},"2":{"en":"Subscribe to a structured online course with flexible deadlines.","hi":"लचीली समय-सीमा वाले व्यवस्थित ऑनलाइन पाठ्यक्रम की सदस्यता लेना।"},"3":{"en":"Attend daily workshops at a local academy.","hi":"स्थानीय अकादमी में प्रतिदिन कार्यशालाओं में जाना।"},"4":{"en":"Wait until he can take long leave and join a studio.","hi":"लंबी छुट्टी लेकर स्टूडियो ज्वाइन करने की प्रतीक्षा करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Ravi needs spare-time study, flexibility and no daily travel<br>An online course with flexible deadlines fits all three needs ✔<br>A full-time diploma and daily workshops clash with his job, and waiting for long leave only postpones the plan<br>Hence he should subscribe to a structured online course with flexible deadlines<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Subscribe to a structured online course with flexible deadlines.</b>","hi":"Ravi को खाली समय में पढ़ाई, लचीलापन तथा प्रतिदिन यात्रा से मुक्ति चाहिए<br>लचीली समय-सीमा वाला ऑनलाइन पाठ्यक्रम तीनों आवश्यकताएँ पूरी करता है ✔<br>पूर्णकालिक डिप्लोमा तथा प्रतिदिन की कार्यशालाएँ उसकी नौकरी से टकराती हैं, और लंबी छुट्टी की प्रतीक्षा योजना को टाल देती है<br>इसलिए उसे लचीली समय-सीमा वाले व्यवस्थित ऑनलाइन पाठ्यक्रम की सदस्यता लेनी चाहिए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): लचीली समय-सीमा वाले व्यवस्थित ऑनलाइन पाठ्यक्रम की सदस्यता लेना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072292","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Match the following Emotional Intelligence dimensions with their characteristics:<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>List I (EI Dimensions)</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>List II (characteristics)</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Self-awareness</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Ability to guide others' emotions and actions</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Self-management</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Being able to sense what others feel and want</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Self-motivation</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Knowledge of true feelings at the moment</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Empathy</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Handling one's emotions to facilitate tasks</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Social skills</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Staying on course towards desired goals</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित भावनात्मक बुद्धि (EI) आयामों को उनकी विशेषताओं से सुमेलित कीजिए:<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>सूची I (EI आयाम)</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>सूची II (विशेषताएँ)</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">आत्म-जागरूकता</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">दूसरों की भावनाओं और कार्यों को दिशा देने की क्षमता</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">आत्म-प्रबंधन</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">दूसरों की भावनाओं और चाहतों को समझ पाना</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">आत्म-प्रेरणा</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">उस क्षण की सच्ची भावनाओं का ज्ञान</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">सहानुभूति</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">कार्यों को सुगम बनाने के लिए अपनी भावनाओं को संभालना</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">सामाजिक कौशल</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">वांछित लक्ष्यों की दिशा में टिके रहना</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"a-iii, b-iv, c-v, d-ii, e-i"},"2":{"en":"a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-v, e-iv"},"3":{"en":"a-v, b-iv, c-ii, d-i, e-iii"},"4":{"en":"a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-v, e-i"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Self-awareness means knowing one's true feelings at the moment, so a–iii ✔<br>Self-management means handling one's emotions to facilitate tasks, so b–iv ✔<br>Self-motivation means staying on course towards desired goals, so c–v ✔<br>Empathy means sensing what others feel and want (d–ii) and social skills mean guiding others' emotions and actions (e–i)<br>Hence a-iii, b-iv, c-v, d-ii, e-i is the correct matching<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): a-iii, b-iv, c-v, d-ii, e-i.</b>","hi":"आत्म-जागरूकता का अर्थ उस क्षण की सच्ची भावनाओं को जानना है, अतः a–iii ✔<br>आत्म-प्रबंधन का अर्थ कार्यों को सुगम बनाने के लिए अपनी भावनाओं को संभालना है, अतः b–iv ✔<br>आत्म-प्रेरणा का अर्थ वांछित लक्ष्यों की दिशा में टिके रहना है, अतः c–v ✔<br>सहानुभूति का अर्थ दूसरों की भावनाएँ और चाहतें समझना (d–ii) तथा सामाजिक कौशल का अर्थ दूसरों की भावनाओं और कार्यों को दिशा देना (e–i) है<br>इसलिए a-iii, b-iv, c-v, d-ii, e-i सही सुमेलन है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): a-iii, b-iv, c-v, d-ii, e-i है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072293","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a group of 120 students, every 8th student knows French, and every 10th knows Spanish. How many students know both the languages? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"120 विद्यार्थियों के समूह में प्रत्येक 8वाँ विद्यार्थी फ्रेंच जानता है तथा प्रत्येक 10वाँ स्पेनिश जानता है। कितने विद्यार्थी दोनों भाषाएँ जानते हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Students who know both must be at positions that are common multiples of 8 and 10<br>The LCM of 8 and 10 is 40, so the common positions are 40, 80 and 120<br>That gives 3 students<br>Hence 3 students know both the languages<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3.</b>","hi":"दोनों भाषाएँ जानने वाले विद्यार्थी वही होंगे जिनके स्थान 8 और 10 के सामान्य गुणज हैं<br>8 और 10 का लघुत्तम समापवर्त्य 40 है, अतः सामान्य स्थान 40, 80 तथा 120 हैं<br>इस प्रकार 3 विद्यार्थी मिलते हैं<br>इसलिए 3 विद्यार्थी दोनों भाषाएँ जानते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072294","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Pick the correct inference:<br>Studies show people who walk daily are less likely to develop heart conditions. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सही अनुमान चुनिए:<br>अध्ययन बताते हैं कि प्रतिदिन पैदल चलने वाले लोगों में हृदय रोग होने की संभावना कम होती है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Walking daily guarantees a healthy heart","hi":"प्रतिदिन चलना स्वस्थ हृदय की गारंटी देता है"},"2":{"en":"Heart health depends solely on walking","hi":"हृदय का स्वास्थ्य केवल चलने पर निर्भर है"},"3":{"en":"People who don't walk are always unhealthy","hi":"जो नहीं चलते वे सदैव अस्वस्थ होते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Regular walking may reduce the risk of heart issues","hi":"नियमित चलना हृदय संबंधी समस्याओं का जोखिम कम कर सकता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The study speaks of a lower likelihood, not of a guarantee and not of a sole cause<br>So the safe inference is that regular walking may reduce the risk of heart issues ✔<br>Guarantee, sole dependence and 'always unhealthy' all overstate the finding<br>Hence regular walking may reduce the risk of heart issues<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Regular walking may reduce the risk of heart issues.</b>","hi":"अध्ययन कम संभावना की बात करता है, गारंटी या एकमात्र कारण की नहीं<br>अतः सुरक्षित अनुमान यह है कि नियमित चलना हृदय संबंधी समस्याओं का जोखिम कम कर सकता है ✔<br>गारंटी, केवल निर्भरता तथा 'सदैव अस्वस्थ' — ये सभी निष्कर्ष को बढ़ा-चढ़ा कर कहते हैं<br>इसलिए नियमित चलना हृदय संबंधी समस्याओं का जोखिम कम कर सकता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): नियमित चलना हृदय संबंधी समस्याओं का जोखिम कम कर सकता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072295","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Examine the first set of figures in Image X. There is a particular relationship between the first and second figures. Using the same connection, select the missing figure from Image Y's options for the second pair.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Image X: (square with a small upright triangle inside) : (triangle with a small shaded square inside) :: (square with a small inverted triangle inside) : ?<br>Image Y: (1) triangle with a small shaded square inside (2) inverted triangle with a small hollow square inside (3) inverted triangle with a small shaded square inside (4) inverted triangle with a small upright triangle inside [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"Image X में आकृतियों के पहले समूह को देखिए। पहली और दूसरी आकृति के बीच एक विशेष संबंध है। उसी संबंध का उपयोग करते हुए दूसरे युग्म के लिए Image Y के विकल्पों में से लुप्त आकृति चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Image X: (वर्ग के भीतर छोटा सीधा त्रिभुज) : (त्रिभुज के भीतर छोटा छायांकित वर्ग) :: (वर्ग के भीतर छोटा उल्टा त्रिभुज) : ?<br>Image Y: (1) त्रिभुज के भीतर छोटा छायांकित वर्ग (2) उल्टे त्रिभुज के भीतर छोटा खोखला वर्ग (3) उल्टे त्रिभुज के भीतर छोटा छायांकित वर्ग (4) उल्टे त्रिभुज के भीतर छोटा सीधा त्रिभुज [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In the first pair the inner shape becomes the outer shape and the outer shape becomes the inner shape, and the inner shape also gets shaded ✔<br>So in the second pair the inner inverted triangle should become the outer shape and the outer square should become the inner shaded square<br>The inverted triangle with a small shaded square inside is figure 3 of Image Y, and the inner shape keeps the same inverted orientation as printed in the key figure<br>Hence the answer is figure 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में भीतरी आकृति बाहरी आकृति बन जाती है और बाहरी आकृति भीतरी आकृति बन जाती है, तथा भीतरी आकृति छायांकित भी हो जाती है ✔<br>अतः दूसरे युग्म में भीतरी उल्टा त्रिभुज बाहरी आकृति बनना चाहिए और बाहरी वर्ग भीतर छोटा छायांकित वर्ग बनना चाहिए<br>उल्टे त्रिभुज के भीतर छोटा छायांकित वर्ग Image Y की आकृति 3 है, और कुंजी वाली आकृति में भीतरी आकृति वही उल्टा रूप रखती है<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति 3 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg"]}},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072296","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Based on the Venn diagram given in the image, how many educated women are employed?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Note: In the Venn diagram, the big circle represents \"Employed women\", the small circle represents \"Backward women\", and the triangle represents \"Educated women\". [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"छवि में दिए गए वेन आरेख के आधार पर, कितनी शिक्षित महिलाएँ रोज़गार प्राप्त हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>नोट: वेन आरेख में बड़ा वृत्त \"रोज़गार प्राप्त महिलाएँ\", छोटा वृत्त \"पिछड़ी महिलाएँ\" तथा त्रिभुज \"शिक्षित महिलाएँ\" दर्शाता है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"22"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"18"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Educated women are the region of the triangle, and employed women are the region of the big circle<br>So the required number is the part common to the triangle and the big circle<br>The printed diagram gives 12 and 6 in this common region, so 12 + 6 = 18<br>Hence 18 educated women are employed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 18.</b>","hi":"शिक्षित महिलाएँ त्रिभुज का क्षेत्र हैं और रोज़गार प्राप्त महिलाएँ बड़े वृत्त का क्षेत्र हैं<br>अतः अभीष्ट संख्या त्रिभुज और बड़े वृत्त के सामान्य भाग में है<br>मुद्रित आरेख में इस सामान्य भाग में 12 तथा 6 दिए हैं, अतः 12 + 6 = 18<br>इसलिए 18 शिक्षित महिलाएँ रोज़गार प्राप्त हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072297","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"In Image X, a set of three figures 1, 2 and 3 shows a sequence of folding a piece of paper. Figure 3 illustrates the process of cutting the folded paper. Select a figure from Image Y that most closely resembles the unfolded form of figure 3.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"Image X में आकृतियों का समूह 1, 2 तथा 3 कागज़ मोड़ने का क्रम दर्शाता है। आकृति 3 मुड़े कागज़ को काटने की प्रक्रिया दर्शाती है। Image Y में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो आकृति 3 के खुलने पर बनने वाले रूप से सर्वाधिक मिलती हो।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The paper is folded twice, so the cut pattern is repeated four times when the paper is opened ✔<br>The cut has a triangle on the left and a U shaped notch at the bottom, so after unfolding the design shows four triangles and matching notches on both edges<br>Among the printed options the figure C shows this symmetric pattern in the same spacing<br>Hence the answer is figure C<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C.</b>","hi":"कागज़ दो बार मोड़ा जाता है, अतः खोलने पर कटा हुआ पैटर्न चार बार दोहराया जाता है ✔<br>कट में बाईं ओर त्रिभुज और नीचे U आकार का कटाव है, अतः खोलने पर दोनों किनारों पर चार त्रिभुज तथा मिलते-जुलते कटाव दिखते हैं<br>मुद्रित विकल्पों में आकृति C यही सममित पैटर्न उसी दूरी के साथ दर्शाती है<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति C है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg"]}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072298","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the appropriate figure from Image Y to follow the pattern in Image X.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Image X shows four figures in which the pinwheel shape turns by a step each time.<br>Image Y: (A), (B), (C), (D) as printed. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"Image X के पैटर्न का पालन करने के लिए Image Y में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Image X में चार आकृतियाँ हैं जिनमें पिनव्हील आकृति हर बार एक चरण घूमती है।<br>Image Y: मुद्रित क्रम के अनुसार (A), (B), (C), (D)। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In Image X the shape keeps the same arms and turns by a fixed angle at every step ✔<br>Carrying the turn forward from the fourth figure of Image X gives the figure in which the arms point as shown in option C<br>The other options turn the arms the wrong way or change the gaps<br>Hence the answer is figure C<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C.</b>","hi":"Image X में आकृति अपनी भुजाएँ वैसी ही रखती है और प्रत्येक चरण में निश्चित कोण से घूमती है ✔<br>Image X की चौथी आकृति से घूर्णन आगे बढ़ाने पर वही आकृति मिलती है जिसमें भुजाएँ विकल्प C जैसी दिखती हैं<br>अन्य विकल्प भुजाओं को गलत दिशा में घुमाते हैं या अंतर बदल देते हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति C है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072299","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the figure that stands out from the rest of the figures in the given image.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई छवि में उस आकृति को चुनिए जो शेष आकृतियों से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In each figure a smaller shape is drawn inside a bigger one<br>(A) square (4 sides) → pentagon (5 sides): +1<br>(B) triangle (3) → square (4): +1<br>(C) pentagon (5) → hexagon (6): +1<br>(D) rhombus (4) → triangle (3): −1<br>Only in D does the inner shape have one side fewer<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): D.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक आकृति में बड़ी आकृति के भीतर छोटी आकृति बनी है<br>(A) वर्ग (4 भुजाएँ) → पंचभुज (5 भुजाएँ): +1<br>(B) त्रिभुज (3) → वर्ग (4): +1<br>(C) पंचभुज (5) → षट्भुज (6): +1<br>(D) समचतुर्भुज (4) → त्रिभुज (3): −1<br>केवल D में भीतरी आकृति की एक भुजा कम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072300","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the figure that is different from the rest of the figures shown in the given image.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>Image: four circles, each with two radii and a small dot in one of the two sectors formed. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई छवि में दर्शाई गई आकृतियों में से उस आकृति को चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]<br>छवि: चार वृत्त, जिनमें से प्रत्येक में दो त्रिज्याएँ तथा बने दो भागों में से एक में छोटा बिंदु है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In figures B, C and D the small dot lies in the sector that is on the left of the two radii and the pair of radii opens in the same direction on turning ✔<br>In figure A the dot sits in the other sector, so the position of the dot relative to the radii is different<br>Hence figure A is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A.</b>","hi":"आकृति B, C तथा D में छोटा बिंदु दोनों त्रिज्याओं के बाईं ओर वाले भाग में है और घुमाने पर त्रिज्याओं का युग्म एक ही दिशा में खुलता है ✔<br>आकृति A में बिंदु दूसरे भाग में है, अतः त्रिज्याओं के सापेक्ष बिंदु की स्थिति भिन्न है<br>इसलिए आकृति A शेष से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): A है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072301","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"In the following question, complete the missing portion of the question figure by selecting from the given answer figures (A), (B), (C) and (D).<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दिए गए उत्तर आकृतियों (A), (B), (C) तथा (D) में से चुनकर प्रश्न आकृति का लुप्त भाग पूरा कीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The question figure is a square divided into four quarters and the missing part is the bottom right quarter<br>The symmetry of the figure shows that the missing quarter must carry the same set of arcs and petals as the opposite quarter, kept in the same orientation<br>Answer figure A supplies exactly these curves in the correct orientation, while the other figures have the curves turned or missing<br>Hence the answer is figure A<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A.</b>","hi":"प्रश्न आकृति एक वर्ग है जो चार भागों में विभाजित है और लुप्त भाग नीचे दाईं ओर का भाग है<br>आकृति की सममिति दर्शाती है कि लुप्त भाग में वही चापें और पंखुड़ियाँ उसी दिशा में होनी चाहिए जो सामने वाले भाग में हैं<br>उत्तर आकृति A ठीक ये वक्र सही दिशा में देती है, जबकि अन्य आकृतियों में वक्र घूमे हुए हैं या अनुपस्थित हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति A है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): A है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072302","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Select the Venn diagram that best illustrates the relationship between the following classes.<br>Bat, Human, Mammals [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह वेन आरेख चुनिए जो निम्नलिखित वर्गों के बीच संबंध को सर्वोत्तम रूप से दर्शाता है।<br>बल्ला (चमगादड़), मानव, स्तनधारी [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Both bat and human are mammals, so bat and human must lie inside the circle of mammals ✔<br>Bat and human are two separate groups with no member common, so their circles must not overlap<br>Option (3) shows exactly this, with a big circle of mammals containing two separate small circles for bat and human<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"बल्ला तथा मानव दोनों स्तनधारी हैं, अतः बल्ला और मानव स्तनधारियों के वृत्त के भीतर होने चाहिए ✔<br>बल्ला और मानव दो अलग समूह हैं जिनका कोई सदस्य साझा नहीं, अतः उनके वृत्त अतिव्यापी नहीं होने चाहिए<br>विकल्प (3) ठीक यही दर्शाती है, जिसमें स्तनधारियों का बड़ा वृत्त दो अलग छोटे वृत्तों (बल्ला तथा मानव) को समेटे है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072303","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"In these type of questions, a set of necessary conditions and qualifications required to be fulfilled by the candidate for a certain vacancy in job/promotion/admission in a college etc, along with the biodata of certain candidates who have applied for the same is given. You are required to evaluate and assess a candidate's eligibility and thereby decide upon the appropriate course of action to taken from among the given alternatives.<br>A hospital is hiring candidates for the role of Clinical Operations Coordinator. The selection will be made based on the following criteria:<br>(i) Age must be between 27 and 40 years as on 01/06/2024.<br>(ii) Must possess a Master's degree in Hospital Administration or MBA in Healthcare Management.<br>(iii) Must have at least 5 years of hospital administration experience.<br>(iv) Must be trained in ERP hospital software.<br>(v) Must be certified in Advanced First Aid or Emergency Response Management.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br>(1) If the candidate has 3–4 years of hospital experience but has worked in a JCI-accredited hospital, a probationary appointment may be offered.<br>(2) If the candidate holds a Postgraduate Diploma (instead of a Master's) but has 6+ year's experience and all other criteria, the case can be referred to the HR Board.<br>'Joseph D'Mello, born September 22, 1982, holds a Master's in Healthcare, 5 year's experience in a private clinic, not trained in ERP, but holds Emergency certification.' [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"इस प्रकार के प्रश्नों में किसी नौकरी/पदोन्नति/कॉलेज में प्रवेश आदि के लिए आवश्यक शर्तें तथा योग्यताएँ, साथ ही आवेदन करने वाले कुछ उम्मीदवारों का बायोडाटा दिया जाता है। आपको उम्मीदवार की पात्रता का मूल्यांकन करना है और दिए गए विकल्पों में से उपयुक्त कार्रवाई चुननी है।<br>एक अस्पताल Clinical Operations Coordinator के पद के लिए उम्मीदवार भर्ती कर रहा है। चयन निम्नलिखित मानदंडों पर होगा:<br>(i) 01/06/2024 को आयु 27 से 40 वर्ष के बीच हो।<br>(ii) Hospital Administration में Master's डिग्री या Healthcare Management में MBA हो।<br>(iii) अस्पताल प्रशासन में कम से कम 5 वर्ष का अनुभव हो।<br>(iv) ERP hospital software में प्रशिक्षित हो।<br>(v) Advanced First Aid या Emergency Response Management में प्रमाणित हो।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br>(1) यदि उम्मीदवार के पास 3–4 वर्ष का अस्पताल अनुभव है परंतु उसने JCI-मान्यता प्राप्त अस्पताल में कार्य किया है, तो परिवीक्षा नियुक्ति दी जा सकती है।<br>(2) यदि उम्मीदवार के पास Master's के स्थान पर Postgraduate Diploma है परंतु 6+ वर्ष का अनुभव तथा शेष सभी मानदंड पूरे हैं, तो मामला HR Board को भेजा जा सकता है।<br>'Joseph D'Mello, जन्म 22 सितंबर 1982, के पास Healthcare में Master's, निजी क्लिनिक में 5 वर्ष का अनुभव, ERP में प्रशिक्षण नहीं, परंतु Emergency प्रमाणपत्र है।' [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Selected","hi":"चयनित"},"2":{"en":"Not Selected","hi":"चयनित नहीं"},"3":{"en":"Refer to HR Board","hi":"HR Board को भेजें"},"4":{"en":"Probation appointment","hi":"परिवीक्षा नियुक्ति"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Age on 01/06/2024 is about 41 years, which is above the upper limit of 40 years ✘<br>The candidate also lacks the ERP training required by condition (iv) ✘<br>Neither exception applies, because the experience is not 3–4 years in a JCI-accredited hospital and the degree is a Master's and not a Postgraduate Diploma<br>Hence the candidate is Not Selected<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Not Selected.</b>","hi":"01/06/2024 को आयु लगभग 41 वर्ष है, जो 40 वर्ष की ऊपरी सीमा से अधिक है ✘<br>उम्मीदवार के पास शर्त (iv) का ERP प्रशिक्षण भी नहीं है ✘<br>कोई भी अपवाद लागू नहीं होता, क्योंकि अनुभव JCI-मान्यता प्राप्त अस्पताल में 3–4 वर्ष नहीं है और डिग्री Master's है, Postgraduate Diploma नहीं<br>इसलिए उम्मीदवार चयनित नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): चयनित नहीं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072304","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Select the dice that can be formed by folding the given sheet in the form of a cube.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई शीट को घन के रूप में मोड़कर बनने वाले पासे चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 2 can be formed","hi":"केवल 2 बन सकता है"},"2":{"en":"Only 3 can be formed","hi":"केवल 3 बन सकता है"},"3":{"en":"None can be formed","hi":"कोई नहीं बन सकता"},"4":{"en":"1 and 4 can be formed","hi":"1 और 4 बन सकते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In the sheet, A F C is a row and D B E is a row, with D above C<br>Faces with one face between them in a row are opposite: A ↔ C and D ↔ E; the remaining pair F ↔ B is also opposite<br>Dice 1 shows A and C together ✘<br>Dice 2 shows D and E together ✘<br>Dice 3 shows D and E together ✘<br>Dice 4 shows F and B together ✘<br>Opposite faces can never be seen together, so none of the dice can be formed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): None can be formed.</b>","hi":"शीट में A F C एक पंक्ति में और D B E एक पंक्ति में है, D, C के ऊपर है<br>एक पंक्ति में बीच में एक फलक छोड़कर आने वाले फलक विपरीत होते हैं: A ↔ C और D ↔ E; शेष जोड़ा F ↔ B भी विपरीत है<br>पासा 1 में A और C साथ दिख रहे हैं ✘<br>पासा 2 में D और E साथ दिख रहे हैं ✘<br>पासा 3 में D और E साथ दिख रहे हैं ✘<br>पासा 4 में F और B साथ दिख रहे हैं ✘<br>विपरीत फलक एक साथ नहीं दिख सकते, अतः कोई भी पासा नहीं बन सकता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): None can be formed है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg"]}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072305","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks (_) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br>b a _ a b _ b a _ a b a b a b _ [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"रिक्त स्थान (_) को निम्नलिखित चार विकल्पों में से एक से इस प्रकार भरिए कि श्रेणी दिए गए क्रम में एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करे।<br>b a _ a b _ b a _ a b a b a b _ [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"abab"},"2":{"en":"baba"},"3":{"en":"aabb"},"4":{"en":"bbaa"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Filling baba gives b a b a b a b a b a b a b a b a b<br>The series then repeats the pair ba again and again in a fixed pattern ✔<br>The other options break the repetition of ba at some place<br>Hence baba completes the series<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): baba.</b>","hi":"baba भरने पर श्रेणी बनती है b a b a b a b a b a b a b a b a b<br>तब श्रेणी में युग्म ba निश्चित पैटर्न में बार-बार दोहराया जाता है ✔<br>अन्य विकल्प कहीं-न-कहीं ba की पुनरावृत्ति तोड़ देते हैं<br>इसलिए baba श्रेणी पूरी करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): baba है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072306","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Defence News","question":{"en":"Who was the Director General of Air operations during Operation Sindoor? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ऑपरेशन सिंदूर के दौरान वायु संचालन महानिदेशक (DG Air Operations) कौन थे? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"AN Pramod","hi":"ए.एन. प्रमोद"},"2":{"en":"A.K Bharti","hi":"ए.के. भारती"},"3":{"en":"S.S. Sharda","hi":"एस.एस. शारदा"},"4":{"en":"Bipin rawat","hi":"बिपिन रावत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – A.K Bharti</b><br><b><u>Air Marshal A.K. Bharti</u></b> was the <b>Director General of Air Operations</b> of the Indian Air Force during <b>Operation Sindoor (May 2025)</b> and briefed the media on the IAF's strikes.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Operation Sindoor was launched on <b>7 May 2025</b> against terror infrastructure in Pakistan and PoK, after the <b>Pahalgam attack (22 April 2025)</b>.<br>• The other DGs who briefed were <b>Lt Gen Rajiv Ghai</b> (DGMO, Army) and <b>Vice Admiral A.N. Pramod</b> (DGNO, Navy).<br>• <b>Gen. Bipin Rawat</b> was India's first <b>Chief of Defence Staff</b> (2020–21).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ए.के. भारती</b><br><b><u>एयर मार्शल ए.के. भारती</u></b> <b>ऑपरेशन सिंदूर (मई 2025)</b> के दौरान भारतीय वायु सेना के <b>वायु संचालन महानिदेशक</b> थे और उन्होंने IAF के हमलों पर मीडिया को जानकारी दी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऑपरेशन सिंदूर <b>पहलगाम हमले (22 अप्रैल 2025)</b> के बाद पाकिस्तान और PoK में आतंकी ढाँचे के विरुद्ध <b>7 मई 2025</b> को शुरू किया गया।<br>• जानकारी देने वाले अन्य महानिदेशक <b>लेफ्टिनेंट जनरल राजीव घई</b> (DGMO, थल सेना) और <b>वाइस एडमिरल ए.एन. प्रमोद</b> (DGNO, नौसेना) थे।<br>• <b>जनरल बिपिन रावत</b> भारत के पहले <b>चीफ ऑफ डिफेंस स्टाफ</b> (2020–21) थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072307","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"If a region has a Net Sown Area (NSA) of 80,000 hectares and a Gross Cropped Area (GCA) of 120,000 hectares, what is the cropping intensity? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि किसी क्षेत्र का निवल बोया गया क्षेत्र (NSA) 80,000 हेक्टेयर और सकल फसल क्षेत्र (GCA) 120,000 हेक्टेयर है, तो फसल गहनता क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"125%"},"2":{"en":"150%"},"3":{"en":"160%"},"4":{"en":"180%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 150%</b><br>\\(\\text{Cropping Intensity} = \\frac{\\text{GCA}}{\\text{NSA}} \\times 100\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{120000}{80000} \\times 100 = 150\\%\\)<br>Cropping intensity = <b><u>150%</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Net Sown Area</b> – area sown at least once in a year; <b>Gross Cropped Area</b> – total area sown counting every season.<br>• Higher cropping intensity means <b>more efficient use of land</b> (multiple cropping).<br>• <b>Punjab</b> has one of the highest cropping intensities in India due to assured irrigation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 150%</b><br>\\(\\text{Cropping Intensity} = \\frac{\\text{GCA}}{\\text{NSA}} \\times 100\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{120000}{80000} \\times 100 = 150\\%\\)<br>फसल गहनता = <b><u>150%</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>निवल बोया गया क्षेत्र</b> – वर्ष में कम से कम एक बार बोया गया क्षेत्र; <b>सकल फसल क्षेत्र</b> – हर मौसम को गिनकर कुल बोया गया क्षेत्र।<br>• अधिक फसल गहनता का अर्थ <b>भूमि का अधिक कुशल उपयोग</b> (बहु-फसलीकरण) है।<br>• सुनिश्चित सिंचाई के कारण <b>पंजाब</b> की फसल गहनता भारत में सबसे अधिक में से है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072308","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: DPSP and Fundamental Duties","question":{"en":"<b>Consider the below statements:</b><br>1. Promotion of international peace is a part of DPSP.<br>2. The DPSPs are enforceable by courts.<br>3. Protection of monuments is a fundamental right.<br><b>Which is/are true?</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>नीचे दिए गए कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:</b><br>1. अंतर्राष्ट्रीय शांति को बढ़ावा देना DPSP का भाग है।<br>2. DPSP न्यायालयों द्वारा प्रवर्तनीय हैं।<br>3. स्मारकों का संरक्षण एक मौलिक अधिकार है।<br><b>कौन-सा/से कथन सत्य है/हैं?</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 2"},"3":{"en":"2 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 2 और 3"},"4":{"en":"1,2 and 3 all","hi":"1, 2 और 3 सभी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Only 1</b><br>Promotion of international peace is in <b>Article 51</b> (DPSP) – true. DPSPs are <b>non-justiciable</b> (Article 37) – false. Protection of monuments is a DPSP under <b>Article 49</b>, not a Fundamental Right – false. Hence <b><u>Only 1</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• DPSPs are in <b>Part IV (Articles 36–51)</b>, borrowed from the <b>Irish Constitution</b>.<br>• Dr. Ambedkar called DPSPs <b>\"novel features\"</b> of the Constitution.<br>• Protecting monuments is also a <b>Fundamental Duty</b> (Article 51A(f) – preserve the rich heritage of our composite culture).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय शांति को बढ़ावा <b>अनुच्छेद 51</b> (DPSP) में है – सत्य। DPSP <b>गैर-न्यायोचित (Non-justiciable)</b> हैं (अनुच्छेद 37) – असत्य। स्मारकों का संरक्षण <b>अनुच्छेद 49</b> के तहत DPSP है, मौलिक अधिकार नहीं – असत्य। अतः <b><u>केवल 1</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• DPSP <b>भाग IV (अनुच्छेद 36–51)</b> में हैं, जो <b>आयरलैंड के संविधान</b> से लिए गए हैं।<br>• डॉ. अंबेडकर ने DPSP को संविधान की <b>\"अनोखी विशेषताएँ\"</b> कहा।<br>• स्मारकों की रक्षा एक <b>मौलिक कर्तव्य</b> से भी जुड़ी है (अनुच्छेद 51A(f) – सामासिक संस्कृति की समृद्ध विरासत का परिरक्षण)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072309","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian city hosted the 2010 Commonwealth Games? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस भारतीय शहर ने 2010 राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों की मेज़बानी की? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई"},"2":{"en":"New Delhi","hi":"नई दिल्ली"},"3":{"en":"Hyderabad","hi":"हैदराबाद"},"4":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – New Delhi</b><br>The <b>XIX Commonwealth Games</b> were held in <b><u>New Delhi</u></b> from <b>3 to 14 October 2010</b>; India finished <b>second</b> with 101 medals (38 gold).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The main venue was the <b>Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium</b>, Delhi; mascot <b>\"Shera\"</b>.<br>• It was the first time India hosted the Commonwealth Games.<br>• The <b>2026</b> Commonwealth Games are being held in <b>Glasgow</b>, Scotland; India will host the <b>2030</b> Games in <b>Ahmedabad</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नई दिल्ली</b><br><b>19वें राष्ट्रमंडल खेल</b> <b>3 से 14 अक्टूबर 2010</b> तक <b><u>नई दिल्ली</u></b> में हुए; भारत 101 पदकों (38 स्वर्ण) के साथ <b>दूसरे</b> स्थान पर रहा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मुख्य स्थल <b>जवाहरलाल नेहरू स्टेडियम</b>, दिल्ली; शुभंकर <b>\"शेरा\"</b>।<br>• भारत ने पहली बार राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों की मेज़बानी की।<br>• <b>2026</b> राष्ट्रमंडल खेल <b>ग्लासगो</b>, स्कॉटलैंड में; भारत <b>2030</b> खेलों की मेज़बानी <b>अहमदाबाद</b> में करेगा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072310","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"<b>Find incorrect pairs of Indian Famous persons with their field :</b><br>1. Kailash Satyarthi: Film Director<br>2. Lala Lajpat Rai: Freedom Fighter<br>3. Murlikant Petkar: Book Writer<br>4. Lata Mangeshkar: Playback Singer [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>प्रसिद्ध भारतीय व्यक्तियों और उनके क्षेत्र के गलत युग्म ज्ञात कीजिए:</b><br>1. कैलाश सत्यार्थी: फ़िल्म निर्देशक<br>2. लाला लाजपत राय: स्वतंत्रता सेनानी<br>3. मुरलीकांत पेटकर: पुस्तक लेखक<br>4. लता मंगेशकर: पार्श्व गायिका [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 3","hi":"1 और 3"},"2":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"3":{"en":"3 only","hi":"केवल 3"},"4":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1 and 3</b><br><b>Kailash Satyarthi</b> is a <b>child rights activist</b> (Nobel Peace Prize 2014), and <b>Murlikant Petkar</b> is India's <b>first Paralympic gold medallist</b> (swimming, 1972). So pairs <b><u>1 and 3</u></b> are incorrect.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Satyarthi founded <b>Bachpan Bachao Andolan</b> (1980); shared the Nobel with <b>Malala Yousafzai</b>.<br>• Petkar received the <b>Padma Shri (2018)</b> and the <b>Arjuna Award (Lifetime, 2024)</b>; the film <b>Chandu Champion</b> is based on his life.<br>• <b>Lala Lajpat Rai</b> – \"Punjab Kesari\"; <b>Lata Mangeshkar</b> – Bharat Ratna (2001).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 1 और 3</b><br><b>कैलाश सत्यार्थी</b> <b>बाल अधिकार कार्यकर्ता</b> (नोबेल शांति पुरस्कार 2014) हैं और <b>मुरलीकांत पेटकर</b> भारत के <b>पहले पैरालंपिक स्वर्ण पदक विजेता</b> (तैराकी, 1972) हैं। अतः युग्म <b><u>1 और 3</u></b> गलत हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सत्यार्थी ने <b>बचपन बचाओ आंदोलन</b> (1980) की स्थापना की; उन्होंने <b>मलाला यूसुफ़ज़ई</b> के साथ नोबेल साझा किया।<br>• पेटकर को <b>पद्म श्री (2018)</b> और <b>अर्जुन पुरस्कार (लाइफटाइम, 2024)</b> मिला; फ़िल्म <b>चंदू चैंपियन</b> उनके जीवन पर आधारित है।<br>• <b>लाला लाजपत राय</b> – \"पंजाब केसरी\"; <b>लता मंगेशकर</b> – भारत रत्न (2001)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072311","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Salient Features of the Constitution","question":{"en":"<b>Match the following Schedules with their subject matter:</b><br><table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px auto;'><tr><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>Column A (Schedule)</th><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>Column B (Subject Matter)</th></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>A. Seventh Schedule</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>1. Languages recognized by the Constitution</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>B. Eighth Schedule</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>2. Distribution of powers between Union and States</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>C. Eleventh Schedule</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>3. Municipalities: Functional items</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>D. Twelfth Schedule</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>4. Panchayats: Functional items</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>निम्नलिखित अनुसूचियों का उनके विषय से मिलान कीजिए:</b><br><table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px auto;'><tr><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>स्तंभ A (अनुसूची)</th><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>स्तंभ B (विषय)</th></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>A. सातवीं अनुसूची</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>1. संविधान द्वारा मान्यता प्राप्त भाषाएँ</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>B. आठवीं अनुसूची</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>2. संघ और राज्यों के बीच शक्तियों का वितरण</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>C. ग्यारहवीं अनुसूची</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>3. नगरपालिकाएँ: कार्यात्मक विषय</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>D. बारहवीं अनुसूची</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>4. पंचायतें: कार्यात्मक विषय</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A–1, B–2, C–3, D–4"},"2":{"en":"A–2, B–1, C–4, D–3"},"3":{"en":"A–4, B–3, C–1, D–2"},"4":{"en":"A–3, B–4, C–2, D–1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – A–2, B–1, C–4, D–3</b><br><b>7<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b> – Union, State and Concurrent Lists (A–2); <b>8<sup>th</sup></b> – 22 languages (B–1); <b>11<sup>th</sup></b> – Panchayats, 29 subjects (C–4); <b>12<sup>th</sup></b> – Municipalities, 18 subjects (D–3). Hence <b><u>A–2, B–1, C–4, D–3</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><ul><li>The Constitution has <b>12 Schedules</b>; originally it had 8.</li><li>Last languages added to the 8<sup>th</sup> Schedule: <b>Bodo, Dogri, Maithili, Santhali</b> (92<sup>nd</sup> Amendment, 2003).</li><li>11<sup>th</sup> Schedule – <b>73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment</b>; 12<sup>th</sup> Schedule – <b>74<sup>th</sup> Amendment</b> (both 1992).</li></ul>","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – A–2, B–1, C–4, D–3</b><br><b>7वीं अनुसूची</b> – संघ, राज्य और समवर्ती सूचियाँ (A–2); <b>8वीं</b> – 22 भाषाएँ (B–1); <b>11वीं</b> – पंचायतें, 29 विषय (C–4); <b>12वीं</b> – नगरपालिकाएँ, 18 विषय (D–3)। अतः <b><u>A–2, B–1, C–4, D–3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><ul><li>संविधान में <b>12 अनुसूचियाँ</b> हैं; मूल रूप से 8 थीं।</li><li>8वीं अनुसूची में अंतिम जोड़ी गई भाषाएँ: <b>बोडो, डोगरी, मैथिली, संथाली</b> (92वाँ संशोधन, 2003)।</li><li>11वीं अनुसूची – <b>73वाँ संशोधन</b>; 12वीं अनुसूची – <b>74वाँ संशोधन</b> (दोनों 1992)।</li></ul>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072312","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Maand, a traditional raga-turned-folk form associated with royal courts, belongs to which Indian state? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मांड, शाही दरबारों से जुड़ी एक पारंपरिक राग से लोक बनी गायन शैली, किस भारतीय राज्य से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"2":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"4":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Rajasthan</b><br><b><u>Maand</u></b> is a semi-classical folk singing style of <b>Rajasthan</b>, which developed in the royal courts and sings of Rajput rulers' valour and love stories.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Famous Maand singer: <b>Allah Jilai Bai</b> of Bikaner, known for <b>\"Kesariya Balam\"</b>.<br>• Other Rajasthan folk forms: <b>Panihari, Pabuji ki Phad, Ghoomar</b> (dance).<br>• Allah Jilai Bai received the <b>Padma Shri</b> in 1982.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – राजस्थान</b><br><b><u>मांड</u></b> <b>राजस्थान</b> की अर्ध-शास्त्रीय लोक गायन शैली है, जो राजदरबारों में विकसित हुई और राजपूत शासकों की वीरता तथा प्रेम-कथाओं का गायन करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रसिद्ध मांड गायिका: बीकानेर की <b>अल्लाह जिलाई बाई</b>, जो <b>\"केसरिया बालम\"</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध हैं।<br>• राजस्थान के अन्य लोक रूप: <b>पनिहारी, पाबूजी की फड़, घूमर</b> (नृत्य)।<br>• अल्लाह जिलाई बाई को 1982 में <b>पद्म श्री</b> मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072313","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements about the tribal dance form ‘Dhimsa’ is/are <b>correct?</b><br>1. Dhimsa originated in Koraput district of Odisha.<br>2. It reflects daily tribal activities such as farming and collecting leaves.<br>3. It is now primarily performed in urban centres of Tamil Nadu. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जनजातीय नृत्य ‘ढिमसा’ के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा/से कथन <b>सही</b> है/हैं?<br>1. ढिमसा की उत्पत्ति ओडिशा के कोरापुट ज़िले में हुई।<br>2. यह खेती और पत्ते एकत्र करने जैसी दैनिक जनजातीय गतिविधियों को दर्शाता है।<br>3. यह अब मुख्य रूप से तमिलनाडु के शहरी केंद्रों में किया जाता है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 2"},"2":{"en":"1,2 and 3","hi":"1, 2 और 3"},"3":{"en":"2 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 2 और 3"},"4":{"en":"1 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1 and 2 only</b><br><b>Dhimsa</b> is a tribal dance from the <b>Koraput</b> region of Odisha, also popular among tribes of <b>Andhra Pradesh (Araku Valley)</b>; its movements depict daily tribal life. It is not a Tamil Nadu urban dance, so statement 3 is wrong: <b><u>1 and 2 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Dhimsa is performed mainly by the <b>Porja (Paroja)</b> and other tribes during festivals and weddings.<br>• Musical instruments used: <b>Dappu, Tudumu, Mohuri</b>.<br>• Other Odisha dances: <b>Odissi</b> (classical), <b>Gotipua, Chhau</b> (Mayurbhanj), <b>Sambalpuri</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1 और 2</b><br><b>ढिमसा</b> ओडिशा के <b>कोरापुट</b> क्षेत्र का जनजातीय नृत्य है, जो <b>आंध्र प्रदेश (अराकू घाटी)</b> की जनजातियों में भी लोकप्रिय है; इसकी मुद्राएँ दैनिक जनजातीय जीवन दर्शाती हैं। यह तमिलनाडु का शहरी नृत्य नहीं है, अतः कथन 3 गलत है: <b><u>केवल 1 और 2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ढिमसा मुख्यतः <b>पोरजा (परजा)</b> और अन्य जनजातियों द्वारा त्योहारों और विवाहों में किया जाता है।<br>• प्रयुक्त वाद्य: <b>डप्पु, तुडुमु, मोहुरी</b>।<br>• ओडिशा के अन्य नृत्य: <b>ओडिसी</b> (शास्त्रीय), <b>गोटीपुआ, छऊ</b> (मयूरभंज), <b>संबलपुरी</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072314","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs is <b>correctly</b> matched regarding the instrument and its region of origin?<br>1. Ravanahatha - Rajasthan<br>2. Pung - Manipur<br>3. Taus - Punjab<br>4. Chenda - Assam [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वाद्ययंत्र और उसके उद्गम क्षेत्र के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है?<br>1. रावणहत्था - राजस्थान<br>2. पुंग - मणिपुर<br>3. ताऊस - पंजाब<br>4. चेंडा - असम [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 3"},"2":{"en":"2 and 4 only","hi":"केवल 2 और 4"},"3":{"en":"1, 2 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 1, 2 और 3"},"4":{"en":"1,2,3 and 4","hi":"1, 2, 3 और 4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 1, 2 and 3 only</b><br><b>Ravanahatha</b> (bowed string) – Rajasthan; <b>Pung</b> (drum) – Manipur; <b>Taus</b> (peacock-shaped bowed instrument) – Punjab. <b>Chenda</b> is a cylindrical drum of <b>Kerala</b>, not Assam. Hence <b><u>1, 2 and 3 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Pung cholom</b> is a dance performed while playing the pung in Manipuri Sankirtana.<br>• Chenda is used in <b>Kathakali</b> and temple festivals of Kerala.<br>• Assam's famous instruments: <b>Pepa</b> (buffalo-horn pipe), <b>Dhol</b> and <b>Gogona</b> (used in Bihu).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – केवल 1, 2 और 3</b><br><b>रावणहत्था</b> (गज वाद्य) – राजस्थान; <b>पुंग</b> (ढोल) – मणिपुर; <b>ताऊस</b> (मोर-आकार का गज वाद्य) – पंजाब। <b>चेंडा</b> <b>केरल</b> का बेलनाकार ढोल है, असम का नहीं। अतः <b><u>केवल 1, 2 और 3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पुंग चोलम</b> मणिपुरी संकीर्तन में पुंग बजाते हुए किया जाने वाला नृत्य है।<br>• चेंडा का उपयोग केरल के <b>कथकली</b> और मंदिर उत्सवों में होता है।<br>• असम के प्रसिद्ध वाद्य: <b>पेपा</b> (भैंस के सींग की बाँसुरी), <b>ढोल</b> और <b>गोगोना</b> (बिहू में प्रयुक्त)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072315","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"The Global Innovation Index (GII) is published by: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वैश्विक नवाचार सूचकांक (GII) किसके द्वारा प्रकाशित किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"United Nations Development Programme (UNDP)","hi":"संयुक्त राष्ट्र विकास कार्यक्रम (UNDP)"},"2":{"en":"World Trade Organization (WTO)","hi":"विश्व व्यापार संगठन (WTO)"},"3":{"en":"World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO)","hi":"विश्व बौद्धिक संपदा संगठन (WIPO)"},"4":{"en":"International Monetary Fund (IMF)","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष (IMF)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO)</b><br>The <b>Global Innovation Index</b> is published annually by the <b><u>World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO)</u></b>, ranking economies on their innovation capabilities.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• WIPO HQ: <b>Geneva, Switzerland</b>; a specialised agency of the UN.<br>• In <b>GII 2025</b>, <b>Switzerland</b> ranked 1<sup>st</sup> and <b>India</b> ranked <b>38<sup>th</sup></b>.<br>• GII was first published in <b>2007</b> by INSEAD.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विश्व बौद्धिक संपदा संगठन (WIPO)</b><br><b>वैश्विक नवाचार सूचकांक</b> प्रतिवर्ष <b><u>विश्व बौद्धिक संपदा संगठन (WIPO)</u></b> द्वारा प्रकाशित किया जाता है, जो अर्थव्यवस्थाओं को उनकी नवाचार क्षमता के आधार पर रैंक करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• WIPO मुख्यालय: <b>जिनेवा, स्विट्ज़रलैंड</b>; यह संयुक्त राष्ट्र की विशिष्ट एजेंसी है।<br>• <b>GII 2025</b> में <b>स्विट्ज़रलैंड</b> पहले और <b>भारत</b> <b>38वें</b> स्थान पर रहा।<br>• GII पहली बार <b>2007</b> में INSEAD द्वारा प्रकाशित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072316","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a major advantage of India’s PSLV (Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle)? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा भारत के PSLV (ध्रुवीय उपग्रह प्रक्षेपण यान) का एक प्रमुख लाभ है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Designed exclusively for crewed space missions","hi":"केवल मानवयुक्त अंतरिक्ष मिशनों के लिए बनाया गया"},"2":{"en":"Specialized in launching satellites only into geostationary orbit","hi":"केवल भूस्थिर कक्षा में उपग्रह प्रक्षेपण में विशेषज्ञ"},"3":{"en":"Able to deploy several satellites into distinct orbits within one launch.","hi":"एक ही प्रक्षेपण में कई उपग्रहों को अलग-अलग कक्षाओं में स्थापित करने में सक्षम।"},"4":{"en":"Requires nuclear propulsion for upper stage separation","hi":"ऊपरी चरण के पृथक्करण के लिए परमाणु प्रणोदन की आवश्यकता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Able to deploy several satellites into distinct orbits within one launch.</b><br>PSLV is ISRO's versatile \"workhorse\". Its restartable fourth stage lets it <b><u>place several satellites into different orbits in a single launch</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>PSLV-C37 (February 2017)</b> launched a record <b>104 satellites</b> in one mission.<br>• PSLV has four stages – alternating <b>solid and liquid</b> (PS1 solid, PS2 liquid Vikas, PS3 solid, PS4 liquid).<br>• It launched <b>Chandrayaan-1 (2008)</b>, <b>Mangalyaan (2013)</b> and <b>Aditya-L1 (2023)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – एक ही प्रक्षेपण में कई उपग्रहों को अलग-अलग कक्षाओं में स्थापित करने में सक्षम।</b><br>PSLV इसरो का बहुमुखी \"वर्कहॉर्स\" है। इसका पुनः-प्रज्वलनीय चौथा चरण इसे <b><u>एक ही प्रक्षेपण में कई उपग्रहों को अलग-अलग कक्षाओं में स्थापित</u></b> करने में सक्षम बनाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>PSLV-C37 (फरवरी 2017)</b> ने एक मिशन में रिकॉर्ड <b>104 उपग्रह</b> प्रक्षेपित किए।<br>• PSLV के चार चरण हैं – बारी-बारी से <b>ठोस और द्रव</b> (PS1 ठोस, PS2 द्रव विकास, PS3 ठोस, PS4 द्रव)।<br>• इसने <b>चंद्रयान-1 (2008)</b>, <b>मंगलयान (2013)</b> और <b>आदित्य-L1 (2023)</b> प्रक्षेपित किए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072317","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Rivers","question":{"en":"<b>Match the following rivers with their originating states:</b><br><table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px auto;'><tr><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>List I (River)</th><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>List II (State)</th></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>A. Mahanadi</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>1. Karnataka</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>B. Kaveri</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>2. Madhya Pradesh</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>C. Krishna</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>3. Chhattisgarh</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>D. Narmada</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>4. Maharashtra</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>निम्नलिखित नदियों का उनके उद्गम राज्यों से मिलान कीजिए:</b><br><table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px auto;'><tr><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>सूची I (नदी)</th><th style='padding:6px 10px;text-align:left;'>सूची II (राज्य)</th></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>A. महानदी</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>1. कर्नाटक</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>B. कावेरी</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>2. मध्य प्रदेश</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>C. कृष्णा</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>3. छत्तीसगढ़</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>D. नर्मदा</td><td style='padding:6px 10px;'>4. महाराष्ट्र</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A–3, B–1, C–4, D–2"},"2":{"en":"A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4"},"3":{"en":"A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4"},"4":{"en":"A-4, B-2, C-3, D-1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – A–3, B–1, C–4, D–2</b><br><b>Mahanadi</b> – Sihawa, Dhamtari (<b>Chhattisgarh</b>); <b>Kaveri</b> – Talakaveri, Brahmagiri hills (<b>Karnataka</b>); <b>Krishna</b> – Mahabaleshwar (<b>Maharashtra</b>); <b>Narmada</b> – Amarkantak (<b>Madhya Pradesh</b>). Hence <b><u>A–3, B–1, C–4, D–2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><ul><li><b>Narmada</b> flows <b>westward</b> through a rift valley into the Arabian Sea.</li><li><b>Hirakud Dam</b> is on the Mahanadi; <b>Krishna Raja Sagar</b> on the Kaveri.</li><li>Mahanadi, Krishna and Kaveri form deltas on the <b>Bay of Bengal</b>.</li></ul>","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – A–3, B–1, C–4, D–2</b><br><b>महानदी</b> – सिहावा, धमतरी (<b>छत्तीसगढ़</b>); <b>कावेरी</b> – तलकावेरी, ब्रह्मगिरि पहाड़ियाँ (<b>कर्नाटक</b>); <b>कृष्णा</b> – महाबलेश्वर (<b>महाराष्ट्र</b>); <b>नर्मदा</b> – अमरकंटक (<b>मध्य प्रदेश</b>)। अतः <b><u>A–3, B–1, C–4, D–2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><ul><li><b>नर्मदा</b> भ्रंश घाटी से होकर <b>पश्चिम</b> की ओर बहकर अरब सागर में गिरती है।</li><li><b>हीराकुंड बाँध</b> महानदी पर और <b>कृष्णराज सागर</b> कावेरी पर है।</li><li>महानदी, कृष्णा और कावेरी <b>बंगाल की खाड़ी</b> में डेल्टा बनाती हैं।</li></ul>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072318","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements regarding population growth and demographic trends in India as per Census data:<br>1.) Kerala recorded the lowest decadal population growth rate (9.4%) during 1991–2001 among all Indian states.<br>2.) During 2001–2011, all six most populous Indian states showed a decadal growth rate higher than the previous decade.<br>3.) The adolescent population (aged 10–19 years) in India constituted approximately 20.9% in 2011, with a higher share of males than females.<br>4.) Puducherry registered a lower decadal population growth in 2001–2011 compared to 1991–2001.<br>Which of the above statements is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जनगणना आँकड़ों के अनुसार भारत में जनसंख्या वृद्धि और जनसांख्यिकीय प्रवृत्तियों के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1.) 1991–2001 के दौरान सभी भारतीय राज्यों में केरल ने सबसे कम दशकीय जनसंख्या वृद्धि दर (9.4%) दर्ज की।<br>2.) 2001–2011 के दौरान सभी छह सर्वाधिक जनसंख्या वाले भारतीय राज्यों ने पिछले दशक से अधिक दशकीय वृद्धि दर दर्शाई।<br>3.) 2011 में भारत में किशोर जनसंख्या (10–19 वर्ष) लगभग 20.9% थी, जिसमें महिलाओं की तुलना में पुरुषों का हिस्सा अधिक था।<br>4.) पुडुचेरी ने 1991–2001 की तुलना में 2001–2011 में कम दशकीय जनसंख्या वृद्धि दर्ज की।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 3"},"2":{"en":"2 and 4 only","hi":"केवल 2 और 4"},"3":{"en":"1, 3 and 4 only","hi":"केवल 1, 3 और 4"},"4":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1 and 3 only</b><br>Statement 1 is correct (Kerala 9.4%). Statement 2 is wrong – the six most populous states (UP, Maharashtra, Bihar, WB, AP, MP) all showed a <b>fall</b> in growth rate in 2001–11. Statement 3 is correct. Statement 4 is wrong – Puducherry's growth <b>rose</b> in 2001–11. Hence <b><u>1 and 3 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India's decadal growth rate in 2001–2011 was <b>17.7%</b>, the lowest since Independence.<br>• Highest growth in 2001–11: <b>Meghalaya</b> (state) and <b>Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli</b> (UT); lowest: <b>Nagaland</b> (negative).<br>• Census 2011 was the <b>15<sup>th</sup></b> Census; sex ratio <b>943</b>, literacy <b>74.04%</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1 और 3</b><br>कथन 1 सही है (केरल 9.4%)। कथन 2 गलत है – छह सर्वाधिक जनसंख्या वाले राज्यों (उ.प्र., महाराष्ट्र, बिहार, प.बं., आं.प्र., म.प्र.) सभी की वृद्धि दर 2001–11 में <b>घटी</b>। कथन 3 सही है। कथन 4 गलत है – पुडुचेरी की वृद्धि 2001–11 में <b>बढ़ी</b>। अतः <b><u>केवल 1 और 3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2001–2011 में भारत की दशकीय वृद्धि दर <b>17.7%</b> थी, जो स्वतंत्रता के बाद सबसे कम थी।<br>• 2001–11 में सर्वाधिक वृद्धि: <b>मेघालय</b> (राज्य) और <b>दादरा व नगर हवेली</b> (UT); सबसे कम: <b>नागालैंड</b> (ऋणात्मक)।<br>• जनगणना 2011 <b>15वीं</b> जनगणना थी; लिंगानुपात <b>943</b>, साक्षरता <b>74.04%</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072319","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following styles is seen in Bombay’s Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (CSMT) Railway Station? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बॉम्बे के छत्रपति शिवाजी महाराज टर्मिनस (CSMT) रेलवे स्टेशन में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी शैली दिखाई देती है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indo-Islamic","hi":"हिंद-इस्लामी"},"2":{"en":"Mughal","hi":"मुग़ल"},"3":{"en":"Gothic Revival","hi":"गॉथिक रिवाइवल"},"4":{"en":"Buddhist","hi":"बौद्ध"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Gothic Revival</b><br>CSMT (formerly Victoria Terminus), designed by <b>F.W. Stevens</b> and completed in <b>1888</b>, is built in the <b><u>Victorian Gothic Revival</u></b> style blended with traditional Indian features.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• CSMT became a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2004</b>.<br>• Other Gothic buildings in Mumbai: <b>Bombay High Court, University of Mumbai (Rajabai Tower)</b>.<br>• The <b>Victorian Gothic and Art Deco Ensembles of Mumbai</b> were inscribed as a World Heritage Site in <b>2018</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – गॉथिक रिवाइवल</b><br><b>एफ.डब्ल्यू. स्टीवंस</b> द्वारा डिज़ाइन और <b>1888</b> में पूर्ण CSMT (पूर्व में विक्टोरिया टर्मिनस) पारंपरिक भारतीय विशेषताओं के साथ <b><u>विक्टोरियन गॉथिक रिवाइवल</u></b> शैली में बना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CSMT <b>2004 में यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल</b> बना।<br>• मुंबई की अन्य गॉथिक इमारतें: <b>बॉम्बे उच्च न्यायालय, मुंबई विश्वविद्यालय (राजाबाई टॉवर)</b>।<br>• <b>मुंबई के विक्टोरियन गॉथिक और आर्ट डेको समूह</b> को <b>2018</b> में विश्व धरोहर स्थल घोषित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072320","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"National Team Chess Championship 2024-25 held in ________. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"राष्ट्रीय टीम शतरंज चैंपियनशिप 2024-25 ________ में आयोजित हुई। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pune","hi":"पुणे"},"2":{"en":"New Delhi","hi":"नई दिल्ली"},"3":{"en":"Chandigarh","hi":"चंडीगढ़"},"4":{"en":"Ahmedabad","hi":"अहमदाबाद"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Ahmedabad</b><br>The <b>National Team Chess Championship 2024-25</b> (men and women) was held in <b><u>Ahmedabad</u></b>, Gujarat, from <b>5 to 11 March 2025</b>, organised under the All India Chess Federation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chess governing body in India: <b>All India Chess Federation (AICF)</b>, HQ <b>Chennai</b>.<br>• India won <b>both open and women's gold</b> at the <b>45<sup>th</sup> Chess Olympiad, Budapest (2024)</b>.<br>• <b>D. Gukesh</b> became the youngest World Chess Champion in December 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – अहमदाबाद</b><br><b>राष्ट्रीय टीम शतरंज चैंपियनशिप 2024-25</b> (पुरुष और महिला) अखिल भारतीय शतरंज महासंघ के अधीन <b>5 से 11 मार्च 2025</b> तक <b><u>अहमदाबाद</u></b>, गुजरात में आयोजित हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में शतरंज का शासी निकाय: <b>अखिल भारतीय शतरंज महासंघ (AICF)</b>, मुख्यालय <b>चेन्नई</b>।<br>• भारत ने <b>45वें शतरंज ओलंपियाड, बुडापेस्ट (2024)</b> में <b>ओपन और महिला दोनों स्वर्ण</b> जीते।<br>• <b>डी. गुकेश</b> दिसंबर 2024 में सबसे कम उम्र के विश्व शतरंज चैंपियन बने।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072321","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"<b>Read the two short statements and choose the correct option.</b><br>1. Victoria Memorial was conceived by Lord Curzon as a tribute to Queen Victoria.<br>2. The monument is built of white Makrana marble in the Indo-Saracenic style. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>दोनों लघु कथनों को पढ़िए और सही विकल्प चुनिए।</b><br>1. विक्टोरिया मेमोरियल की परिकल्पना लॉर्ड कर्ज़न ने महारानी विक्टोरिया को श्रद्धांजलि के रूप में की थी।<br>2. यह स्मारक सफ़ेद मकराना संगमरमर से इंडो-सारसेनिक शैली में बना है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>The <b>Victoria Memorial, Kolkata</b> was conceived by <b>Lord Curzon</b> after Queen Victoria's death (1901). It was designed by <b>William Emerson</b> in <b>Indo-Saracenic</b> style using <b>white Makrana marble</b>. Both are correct: <b><u>Both 1 and 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The foundation stone was laid in <b>1906</b> by the Prince of Wales; it opened in <b>1921</b>.<br>• Makrana marble comes from <b>Nagaur district, Rajasthan</b> (also used in the Taj Mahal).<br>• Today it is a <b>museum</b> under the Ministry of Culture.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br><b>विक्टोरिया मेमोरियल, कोलकाता</b> की परिकल्पना महारानी विक्टोरिया की मृत्यु (1901) के बाद <b>लॉर्ड कर्ज़न</b> ने की। इसे <b>विलियम एमर्सन</b> ने <b>सफ़ेद मकराना संगमरमर</b> से <b>इंडो-सारसेनिक</b> शैली में डिज़ाइन किया। दोनों सही हैं: <b><u>1 और 2 दोनों</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी आधारशिला <b>1906</b> में प्रिंस ऑफ वेल्स ने रखी; यह <b>1921</b> में खुला।<br>• मकराना संगमरमर <b>नागौर ज़िला, राजस्थान</b> से आता है (ताजमहल में भी प्रयुक्त)।<br>• आज यह संस्कृति मंत्रालय के अधीन एक <b>संग्रहालय</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072322","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Rivers","question":{"en":"Which of the following is considered the largest river system among the Deccan rivers in India? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत में दक्कन की नदियों में निम्नलिखित में से किसे सबसे बड़ा नदी तंत्र माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cauvery","hi":"कावेरी"},"2":{"en":"Krishna","hi":"कृष्णा"},"3":{"en":"Godavari","hi":"गोदावरी"},"4":{"en":"Mahanadi","hi":"महानदी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Godavari</b><br>The <b><u>Godavari</u></b> is the largest Peninsular river system (about <b>1,465 km</b>), rising at <b>Trimbakeshwar, Nashik</b>; it is called the <b>\"Dakshin Ganga\"</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• About <b>49%</b> of the Godavari basin lies in <b>Maharashtra</b>.<br>• Main tributaries: <b>Penganga, Wardha, Wainganga, Indravati, Manjra</b>.<br>• <b>Krishna</b> is the second-largest east-flowing Peninsular river.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – गोदावरी</b><br><b><u>गोदावरी</u></b> सबसे बड़ा प्रायद्वीपीय नदी तंत्र (लगभग <b>1,465 km</b>) है, जो <b>त्र्यंबकेश्वर, नासिक</b> से निकलती है; इसे <b>\"दक्षिण गंगा\"</b> कहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गोदावरी बेसिन का लगभग <b>49%</b> भाग <b>महाराष्ट्र</b> में है।<br>• प्रमुख सहायक नदियाँ: <b>पेनगंगा, वर्धा, वैनगंगा, इंद्रावती, मांजरा</b>।<br>• <b>कृष्णा</b> दूसरी सबसे बड़ी पूर्व-वाहिनी प्रायद्वीपीय नदी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072323","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"According to BNSS, what does the term \"bail\" mean? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"BNSS के अनुसार \"ज़मानत\" शब्द का क्या अर्थ है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arrest under judicial supervision","hi":"न्यायिक पर्यवेक्षण में गिरफ़्तारी"},"2":{"en":"Police custody under specific terms","hi":"विशिष्ट शर्तों पर पुलिस अभिरक्षा"},"3":{"en":"Release from custody on conditions imposed by Court or officer","hi":"न्यायालय या अधिकारी द्वारा लगाई गई शर्तों पर अभिरक्षा से रिहाई"},"4":{"en":"Removal of charges before trial","hi":"विचारण से पहले आरोपों को हटाना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Release from custody on conditions imposed by Court or officer</b><br><b>Section 2(1)(b) of BNSS, 2023</b> defines bail as the <b><u>release of a person accused or suspected of an offence from the custody of law upon conditions imposed by an officer or Court</u></b>, on execution of a bond or bail bond.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The old CrPC, 1973 did <b>not define</b> \"bail\"; BNSS defined it for the first time.<br>• BNSS also defines <b>\"bail bond\"</b> (with surety) and <b>\"bond\"</b> (personal bond without surety).<br>• BNSS came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>, replacing CrPC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – न्यायालय या अधिकारी द्वारा लगाई गई शर्तों पर अभिरक्षा से रिहाई</b><br><b>BNSS, 2023 की धारा 2(1)(b)</b> ज़मानत को किसी अपराध के अभियुक्त या संदिग्ध व्यक्ति की <b><u>किसी अधिकारी या न्यायालय द्वारा लगाई गई शर्तों पर विधि की अभिरक्षा से रिहाई</u></b> के रूप में परिभाषित करती है, जो बंधपत्र या ज़मानत बंधपत्र निष्पादित करने पर होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पुरानी CrPC, 1973 में \"ज़मानत\" की <b>परिभाषा नहीं</b> थी; BNSS ने पहली बार इसे परिभाषित किया।<br>• BNSS <b>\"ज़मानत बंधपत्र\"</b> (प्रतिभू सहित) और <b>\"बंधपत्र\"</b> (बिना प्रतिभू का व्यक्तिगत बंधपत्र) को भी परिभाषित करती है।<br>• BNSS <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से CrPC के स्थान पर लागू हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072324","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Solar System","question":{"en":"Which of the following does not belong to the solar system? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन सौरमंडल से संबंधित नहीं है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Planet","hi":"ग्रह"},"2":{"en":"Galaxy","hi":"आकाशगंगा"},"3":{"en":"Meteor","hi":"उल्का"},"4":{"en":"Comet","hi":"धूमकेतु"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Galaxy</b><br>Planets, meteors and comets are members of the solar system. A <b><u>galaxy</u></b> is a huge system of billions of stars; our solar system itself lies inside the <b>Milky Way galaxy</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The nearest major galaxy to the Milky Way is <b>Andromeda</b>.<br>• <b>Comets</b> come mainly from the <b>Kuiper Belt</b> and <b>Oort Cloud</b>; Halley's Comet appears every ~76 years.<br>• A <b>meteor</b> is a \"shooting star\"; a piece that reaches the ground is a <b>meteorite</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – आकाशगंगा</b><br>ग्रह, उल्काएँ और धूमकेतु सौरमंडल के सदस्य हैं। <b><u>आकाशगंगा (Galaxy)</u></b> अरबों तारों का विशाल तंत्र है; हमारा सौरमंडल स्वयं <b>मंदाकिनी (Milky Way) आकाशगंगा</b> के भीतर स्थित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मंदाकिनी के सबसे निकट प्रमुख आकाशगंगा <b>एंड्रोमेडा</b> है।<br>• <b>धूमकेतु</b> मुख्यतः <b>काइपर बेल्ट</b> और <b>ऊर्ट बादल</b> से आते हैं; हैली धूमकेतु लगभग 76 वर्ष में दिखता है।<br>• <b>उल्का</b> \"टूटता तारा\" है; ज़मीन तक पहुँचने वाला टुकड़ा <b>उल्कापिंड (Meteorite)</b> कहलाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072325","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a scalar quantity? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी अदिश राशि है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Displacement","hi":"विस्थापन"},"2":{"en":"Velocity","hi":"वेग"},"3":{"en":"Acceleration","hi":"त्वरण"},"4":{"en":"Speed","hi":"चाल"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Speed</b><br>A scalar has only magnitude. <b><u>Speed</u></b> is a scalar, while displacement, velocity and acceleration are <b>vectors</b> (they have both magnitude and direction).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Scalars: <b>mass, distance, speed, time, work, energy, temperature</b>.<br>• Vectors: <b>displacement, velocity, acceleration, force, momentum, torque</b>.<br>• Speed = distance/time; Velocity = displacement/time; SI unit of both is <b>m/s</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – चाल</b><br>अदिश राशि में केवल परिमाण होता है। <b><u>चाल (Speed)</u></b> अदिश है, जबकि विस्थापन, वेग और त्वरण <b>सदिश (Vector)</b> हैं (इनमें परिमाण और दिशा दोनों होते हैं)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अदिश: <b>द्रव्यमान, दूरी, चाल, समय, कार्य, ऊर्जा, ताप</b>।<br>• सदिश: <b>विस्थापन, वेग, त्वरण, बल, संवेग, बल-आघूर्ण</b>।<br>• चाल = दूरी/समय; वेग = विस्थापन/समय; दोनों का SI मात्रक <b>m/s</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072326","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"What does BIMSTEC stand for? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"BIMSTEC का पूर्ण रूप क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bay of Islands Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation","hi":"बे ऑफ आइलैंड्स मल्टी-सेक्टोरल टेक्निकल एंड इकोनॉमिक कोऑपरेशन"},"2":{"en":"Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation","hi":"बहु-क्षेत्रीय तकनीकी और आर्थिक सहयोग हेतु बंगाल की खाड़ी पहल"},"3":{"en":"Bangladesh, India, Myanmar, Sri Lanka, Thailand, Egypt, and China","hi":"बांग्लादेश, भारत, म्यांमार, श्रीलंका, थाईलैंड, मिस्र और चीन"},"4":{"en":"Bay of Bengal International Maritime Security and Trade Council","hi":"बंगाल की खाड़ी अंतर्राष्ट्रीय समुद्री सुरक्षा और व्यापार परिषद"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation</b><br>BIMSTEC stands for <b><u>Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation</u></b>, a regional group of seven countries around the Bay of Bengal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Members: <b>Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Myanmar, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Thailand</b>.<br>• Formed in <b>1997</b> by the <b>Bangkok Declaration</b>; secretariat in <b>Dhaka</b>.<br>• The <b>6<sup>th</sup> BIMSTEC Summit</b> was held in <b>Bangkok (April 2025)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बहु-क्षेत्रीय तकनीकी और आर्थिक सहयोग हेतु बंगाल की खाड़ी पहल</b><br>BIMSTEC का पूर्ण रूप <b><u>बहु-क्षेत्रीय तकनीकी और आर्थिक सहयोग हेतु बंगाल की खाड़ी पहल (Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation)</u></b> है, जो बंगाल की खाड़ी के आसपास के सात देशों का क्षेत्रीय समूह है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सदस्य: <b>बांग्लादेश, भूटान, भारत, म्यांमार, नेपाल, श्रीलंका, थाईलैंड</b>।<br>• <b>1997</b> में <b>बैंकॉक घोषणा</b> द्वारा गठित; सचिवालय <b>ढाका</b> में।<br>• <b>छठा BIMSTEC शिखर सम्मेलन</b> <b>बैंकॉक (अप्रैल 2025)</b> में हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072327","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"Which of the following monuments was NOT built by Emperor Shah Jahan? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा स्मारक सम्राट शाहजहाँ द्वारा नहीं बनवाया गया था? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Taj Mahal","hi":"ताजमहल"},"2":{"en":"Red Fort, Delhi","hi":"लाल किला, दिल्ली"},"3":{"en":"Jama Masjid, Delhi","hi":"जामा मस्जिद, दिल्ली"},"4":{"en":"Humayun's Tomb","hi":"हुमायूँ का मकबरा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Humayun's Tomb</b><br><b><u>Humayun's Tomb</u></b> (Delhi) was built by Humayun's widow <b>Bega Begum (Haji Begum)</b> during <b>Akbar's</b> reign (completed 1572). The other three were built by Shah Jahan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Humayun's Tomb was designed by Persian architect <b>Mirak Mirza Ghiyas</b>; it is the first <b>garden-tomb</b> in India (UNESCO site, 1993).<br>• Shah Jahan's other works: <b>Moti Masjid (Agra), Shalimar Bagh (Lahore), Peacock Throne</b>.<br>• Shah Jahan founded <b>Shahjahanabad</b> (Old Delhi) in 1639.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – हुमायूँ का मकबरा</b><br><b><u>हुमायूँ का मकबरा</u></b> (दिल्ली) <b>अकबर</b> के शासनकाल में हुमायूँ की विधवा <b>बेगा बेगम (हाजी बेगम)</b> ने बनवाया (1572 में पूर्ण)। अन्य तीनों शाहजहाँ ने बनवाए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• हुमायूँ के मकबरे के वास्तुकार फ़ारसी <b>मीरक मिर्ज़ा ग़ियास</b> थे; यह भारत का पहला <b>उद्यान-मकबरा</b> है (यूनेस्को स्थल, 1993)।<br>• शाहजहाँ की अन्य कृतियाँ: <b>मोती मस्जिद (आगरा), शालीमार बाग़ (लाहौर), मयूर सिंहासन</b>।<br>• शाहजहाँ ने 1639 में <b>शाहजहाँनाबाद</b> (पुरानी दिल्ली) बसाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072328","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"The procedure for impeachment of the President of India is laid down under Article ________ of the Indian Constitution. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रपति पर महाभियोग की प्रक्रिया भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद ________ में दी गई है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"59"},"2":{"en":"60"},"3":{"en":"61"},"4":{"en":"62"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 61</b><br><b><u>Article 61</u></b> lays down the procedure for impeachment of the President for <b>\"violation of the Constitution\"</b>. The charge must be passed by a <b>two-thirds majority of the total membership</b> of each House.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>14 days' notice</b> signed by at least <b>one-fourth</b> of the members of the House is required.<br>• No President of India has been impeached so far.<br>• <b>Article 59</b> – conditions of office; <b>Article 60</b> – oath; <b>Article 62</b> – time of election to fill vacancy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 61</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 61</u></b> <b>\"संविधान का उल्लंघन\"</b> करने पर राष्ट्रपति के महाभियोग की प्रक्रिया बताता है। आरोप प्रत्येक सदन की <b>कुल सदस्य संख्या के दो-तिहाई बहुमत</b> से पारित होना चाहिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सदन के कम से कम <b>एक-चौथाई</b> सदस्यों द्वारा हस्ताक्षरित <b>14 दिन का नोटिस</b> आवश्यक है।<br>• अब तक भारत के किसी राष्ट्रपति पर महाभियोग नहीं चला।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 59</b> – पद की शर्तें; <b>अनुच्छेद 60</b> – शपथ; <b>अनुच्छेद 62</b> – रिक्ति भरने हेतु चुनाव का समय।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072329","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"Under PMMY, a business planning to start a tailoring shop should approach which financial body for credit? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"PMMY के तहत सिलाई की दुकान शुरू करने की योजना बना रहे व्यवसाय को ऋण के लिए किस वित्तीय संस्था से संपर्क करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RBI"},"2":{"en":"MUDRA Bank","hi":"मुद्रा बैंक"},"3":{"en":"NABARD","hi":"नाबार्ड"},"4":{"en":"SEBI","hi":"सेबी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – MUDRA Bank</b><br>Under the <b>Pradhan Mantri MUDRA Yojana (PMMY)</b>, loans for small non-farm micro enterprises like a tailoring shop are refinanced through <b><u>MUDRA (Micro Units Development &amp; Refinance Agency)</u></b>, via banks, NBFCs and MFIs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• PMMY was launched on <b>8 April 2015</b>; MUDRA is a subsidiary of <b>SIDBI</b>.<br>• Loan categories: <b>Shishu</b> (up to ₹50,000), <b>Kishore</b> (up to ₹5 lakh), <b>Tarun</b> (up to ₹10 lakh), <b>Tarun Plus</b> (up to ₹20 lakh, from 2024).<br>• Loans under PMMY are <b>collateral-free</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मुद्रा बैंक</b><br><b>प्रधानमंत्री मुद्रा योजना (PMMY)</b> के तहत सिलाई की दुकान जैसे छोटे गैर-कृषि सूक्ष्म उद्यमों के ऋण का पुनर्वित्त <b><u>मुद्रा (Micro Units Development &amp; Refinance Agency)</u></b> द्वारा बैंकों, NBFC और MFI के माध्यम से किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• PMMY <b>8 अप्रैल 2015</b> को शुरू हुई; मुद्रा <b>SIDBI</b> की सहायक संस्था है।<br>• ऋण श्रेणियाँ: <b>शिशु</b> (₹50,000 तक), <b>किशोर</b> (₹5 लाख तक), <b>तरुण</b> (₹10 लाख तक), <b>तरुण प्लस</b> (₹20 लाख तक, 2024 से)।<br>• PMMY के ऋण <b>संपार्श्विक-मुक्त (Collateral-free)</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072330","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who has been appointed as the Chairman of the 16<sup>th</sup> Finance Commission of India (2023–2028)? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के 16वें वित्त आयोग (2023–2028) के अध्यक्ष के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"N. K. Singh","hi":"एन. के. सिंह"},"2":{"en":"Suman Bery","hi":"सुमन बेरी"},"3":{"en":"Arvind Panagariya","hi":"अरविंद पनगढ़िया"},"4":{"en":"Raghuram Rajan","hi":"रघुराम राजन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Arvind Panagariya</b><br><b><u>Dr. Arvind Panagariya</u></b>, former Vice-Chairman of NITI Aayog, was appointed Chairman of the <b>16<sup>th</sup> Finance Commission</b>, constituted on <b>31 December 2023</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 16<sup>th</sup> FC's recommendations cover the award period <b>2026–27 to 2030–31</b>; its report was submitted in <b>November 2025</b>.<br>• Finance Commission is a constitutional body under <b>Article 280</b>.<br>• <b>N.K. Singh</b> chaired the 15<sup>th</sup> FC; <b>Suman Bery</b> is the Vice-Chairman of NITI Aayog.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अरविंद पनगढ़िया</b><br>नीति आयोग के पूर्व उपाध्यक्ष <b><u>डॉ. अरविंद पनगढ़िया</u></b> को <b>31 दिसंबर 2023</b> को गठित <b>16वें वित्त आयोग</b> का अध्यक्ष नियुक्त किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 16वें वित्त आयोग की सिफारिशें <b>2026–27 से 2030–31</b> की अवधि के लिए हैं; इसकी रिपोर्ट <b>नवंबर 2025</b> में सौंपी गई।<br>• वित्त आयोग <b>अनुच्छेद 280</b> के तहत संवैधानिक निकाय है।<br>• <b>एन.के. सिंह</b> 15वें वित्त आयोग के अध्यक्ष थे; <b>सुमन बेरी</b> नीति आयोग के उपाध्यक्ष हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072331","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"A number x = 0.363636... + \\(\\frac{5}{12}\\) is expressed as a simplified fraction \\(\\frac{p}{q}\\). What is the value of p + q? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक संख्या x = 0.363636... + \\(\\frac{5}{12}\\) को सरलतम भिन्न \\(\\frac{p}{q}\\) के रूप में व्यक्त किया जाता है। p + q का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"230"},"2":{"en":"235"},"3":{"en":"240"},"4":{"en":"220"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(0.363636... = \\frac{36}{99} = \\frac{4}{11}\\)<br>\\(x = \\frac{4}{11} + \\frac{5}{12} = \\frac{48 + 55}{132} = \\frac{103}{132}\\)<br>\\(p + q = 103 + 132 = \\boxed{235}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 235.</b>","hi":"\\(0.363636... = \\frac{36}{99} = \\frac{4}{11}\\)<br>\\(x = \\frac{4}{11} + \\frac{5}{12} = \\frac{48 + 55}{132} = \\frac{103}{132}\\)<br>\\(p + q = 103 + 132 = \\boxed{235}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 235 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072332","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Two real numbers together produce a total of 9. The total of their squared values is 45. Determine the multiplication outcome of the two numbers. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो वास्तविक संख्याओं का योग 9 है। उनके वर्गों का योग 45 है। दोनों संख्याओं का गुणनफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"21"},"4":{"en":"14"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(a + b = 9\\), \\(a^2 + b^2 = 45\\)<br>\\(ab = \\frac{(a+b)^2 - (a^2+b^2)}{2} = \\frac{81 - 45}{2}\\)<br>\\(ab = \\boxed{18}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 18.</b>","hi":"\\(a + b = 9\\), \\(a^2 + b^2 = 45\\)<br>\\(ab = \\frac{(a+b)^2 - (a^2+b^2)}{2} = \\frac{81 - 45}{2}\\)<br>\\(ab = \\boxed{18}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072333","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A certain amount becomes ₹27,000 in 3 years when compounded annually. It is known that the cube root of the amount and the square root of the principal are both natural numbers. What is the rate of interest per annum? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कोई धनराशि वार्षिक रूप से चक्रवृद्धि होकर 3 वर्षों में ₹27,000 हो जाती है। यह ज्ञात है कि राशि का घनमूल और मूलधन का वर्गमूल दोनों प्राकृत संख्याएँ हैं। प्रति वर्ष ब्याज दर क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10%"},"2":{"en":"15%"},"3":{"en":"20%"},"4":{"en":"25%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Given:</b> \\(A = 27000 = 30^3\\) (cube root is 30 ✓). \\(\\sqrt{P}\\) must be a natural number, so \\(P\\) is a perfect square.<br><br><b>Formula:</b> \\(P = \\frac{A}{(1 + r)^3}\\)<br><br>Since \\(A = 27000 = 3^3 \\times 10^3\\) is a perfect cube, \\(P\\) will be a whole number when \\((1 + r)\\) is a simple fraction like \\(\\frac{6}{5}\\).<br><br>Take \\(r = 20\\% = \\frac{1}{5}\\), so \\(1 + r = \\frac{6}{5}\\)<br>\\(P = 27000 \\times \\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^3 = 27000 \\times \\frac{125}{216} = 125 \\times 125 = 15625\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{15625} = 125\\), a natural number ✓<br><br><b>Verification:</b> \\(15625 \\times \\frac{6}{5} \\times \\frac{6}{5} \\times \\frac{6}{5} = 27000\\) ✓<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 20%.</b>","hi":"<b>दिया है:</b> \\(A = 27000 = 30^3\\) (घनमूल 30 है ✓)। \\(\\sqrt{P}\\) प्राकृत संख्या होनी चाहिए, अतः \\(P\\) एक पूर्ण वर्ग है।<br><br><b>सूत्र:</b> \\(P = \\frac{A}{(1 + r)^3}\\)<br><br>चूँकि \\(A = 27000 = 3^3 \\times 10^3\\) एक पूर्ण घन है, इसलिए \\((1 + r)\\) जब \\(\\frac{6}{5}\\) जैसा सरल भिन्न होगा तो \\(P\\) पूर्ण संख्या आएगा।<br><br>\\(r = 20\\% = \\frac{1}{5}\\) लेने पर \\(1 + r = \\frac{6}{5}\\)<br>\\(P = 27000 \\times \\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^3 = 27000 \\times \\frac{125}{216} = 125 \\times 125 = 15625\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{15625} = 125\\), एक प्राकृत संख्या ✓<br><br><b>जाँच:</b> \\(15625 \\times \\frac{6}{5} \\times \\frac{6}{5} \\times \\frac{6}{5} = 27000\\) ✓<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 20% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072334","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Using the information in the pie chart, answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q54.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If a total of ₹12,00,000 was invested across all sectors shown in the pie chart, how much more was spent on EdTech than on AR/VR Learning? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पाई चार्ट में दी गई जानकारी का उपयोग करके निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दें।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q54.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि पाई चार्ट में दर्शाए गए सभी क्षेत्रों में कुल ₹12,00,000 निवेश किए गए, तो EdTech पर AR/VR Learning की तुलना में कितना अधिक खर्च किया गया? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1,20,000"},"2":{"en":"₹1,50,000"},"3":{"en":"₹1,80,000"},"4":{"en":"₹2,00,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Difference of shares \\(= 40\\% - 25\\% = 15\\%\\)<br>\\(= 15\\%\\) of ₹12,00,000 \\(= 0.15 \\times 12{,}00{,}000\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{1{,}80{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹1,80,000.</b>","hi":"हिस्सों का अंतर \\(= 40\\% - 25\\% = 15\\%\\)<br>₹\\(= 12,00,000\\) का 15% \\(= 0.15 \\times 12{,}00{,}000\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{1{,}80{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹1,80,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q54.jpg"]}},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072335","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Consider an arbitrary triangle ABC. Which of the following statements about its centers is always true, regardless of the type of triangle (e.g., equilateral, isosceles, right-angled, scalene)? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक स्वेच्छ त्रिभुज ABC पर विचार कीजिए। इसके केंद्रों के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन त्रिभुज के प्रकार (जैसे समबाहु, समद्विबाहु, समकोण, विषमबाहु) की परवाह किए बिना सदैव सत्य है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The incenter, circumcenter, centroid, and orthocenter all coincide.","hi":"अंतःकेंद्र, परिकेंद्र, केंद्रक और लंबकेंद्र सभी संपाती होते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"The orthocenter is always located inside the triangle.","hi":"लंबकेंद्र सदैव त्रिभुज के भीतर स्थित होता है।"},"3":{"en":"The incenter is equidistant from all sides of the triangle.","hi":"अंतःकेंद्र त्रिभुज की सभी भुजाओं से समान दूरी पर होता है।"},"4":{"en":"The circumcenter is equidistant from all vertices of the triangle and is always inside the triangle.","hi":"परिकेंद्र त्रिभुज के सभी शीर्षों से समान दूरी पर होता है और सदैव त्रिभुज के भीतर होता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Option (a) holds only for equilateral triangles<br>Option (b) fails for an obtuse triangle (orthocenter lies outside)<br>Option (d) fails for an obtuse triangle (circumcenter lies outside)<br>The incenter is the centre of the incircle, so it is always equidistant from the three sides<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{The incenter is equidistant from all sides of the triangle}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The incenter is equidistant from all sides of the triangle.</b>","hi":"विकल्प (a) केवल समबाहु त्रिभुज के लिए सत्य है<br>विकल्प (b) अधिक कोण त्रिभुज में असत्य है (लंबकेंद्र बाहर होता है)<br>विकल्प (d) अधिक कोण त्रिभुज में असत्य है (परिकेंद्र बाहर होता है)<br>अंतःकेंद्र अंतःवृत्त का केंद्र है, अतः वह सदैव तीनों भुजाओं से समान दूरी पर होता है<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{अंतःकेंद्र त्रिभुज की सभी भुजाओं से समान दूरी पर होता है}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): अंतःकेंद्र त्रिभुज की सभी भुजाओं से समान दूरी पर होता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072336","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"40 men can complete a job in 30 days. 60 men start the work and continue for x days. Then 20 men leave, and the remaining men complete the work in 9 days. Find the value of x. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"40 आदमी किसी कार्य को 30 दिनों में पूरा कर सकते हैं। 60 आदमी कार्य शुरू करते हैं और x दिनों तक कार्य करते हैं। फिर 20 आदमी चले जाते हैं और शेष आदमी कार्य 9 दिनों में पूरा करते हैं। x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"13"},"3":{"en":"14"},"4":{"en":"15"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Total work \\(= 40 \\times 30 = 1200\\) man-days<br>\\(60x + 40 \\times 9 = 1200 \\Rightarrow 60x = 840\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{14}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 14.</b>","hi":"कुल कार्य \\(= 40 \\times 30 = 1200\\) आदमी-दिन<br>\\(60x + 40 \\times 9 = 1200 \\Rightarrow 60x = 840\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{14}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 14 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072337","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The radius of a cylinder is increased by 20%, height decreased by 10%. Find approximate percentage change in volume. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बेलन की त्रिज्या 20% बढ़ाई जाती है और ऊँचाई 10% घटाई जाती है। आयतन में अनुमानित प्रतिशत परिवर्तन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25.6% increase","hi":"25.6% वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"29.6% increase","hi":"29.6% वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"18% decrease","hi":"18% कमी"},"4":{"en":"12% decrease","hi":"12% कमी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Volume \\(\\propto r^2h\\)<br>Factor \\(= (1.2)^2 \\times 0.9 = 1.44 \\times 0.9 = 1.296\\)<br>Change \\(= \\boxed{29.6\\%\\ \\text{increase}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 29.6% increase.</b>","hi":"आयतन \\(\\propto r^2h\\)<br>गुणक \\(= (1.2)^2 \\times 0.9 = 1.44 \\times 0.9 = 1.296\\)<br>परिवर्तन \\(= \\boxed{29.6\\%\\ \\text{वृद्धि}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 29.6% वृद्धि है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072338","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A regular square pyramid having a base side length of 18 m. If its total surface area is 864 m², and its slant height is 15 m, find the height of the pyramid. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक सम वर्गाकार पिरामिड की आधार भुजा की लंबाई 18 m है। यदि उसका कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 864 m² है और तिर्यक ऊँचाई 15 m है, तो पिरामिड की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 m"},"2":{"en":"10 m"},"3":{"en":"12 m"},"4":{"en":"14 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"252\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 252 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L126 26L226 159ZM133 159L133 152L126 152\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M126 26L126 159\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"159\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"121\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">h</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"78\">l = 15 m</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"11\">a/2 = 9 m</text></g></svg><br>TSA \\(= 18^2 + 4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times 18 \\times 15 = 324 + 540 = 864\\) ✓<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{l^2 - \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2}\\)<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{144} = \\boxed{12\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"252\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 252 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L126 26L226 159ZM133 159L133 152L126 152\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M126 26L126 159\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"159\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"121\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">h</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"78\">l = 15 m</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"11\">a/2 = 9 m</text></g></svg><br>कुल पृष्ठ \\(= 18^2 + 4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times 18 \\times 15 = 324 + 540 = 864\\) ✓<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{l^2 - \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2}\\)<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{144} = \\boxed{12\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072339","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A regular square pyramid has a volume of 384 cm³ and its height-to-base-edge ratio is 2:3. Find the radius of the sphere inscribed within it. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक सम वर्गाकार पिरामिड का आयतन 384 cm³ है और उसकी ऊँचाई तथा आधार भुजा का अनुपात 2:3 है। उसमें अंतर्निहित गोले की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 cm"},"2":{"en":"4 cm"},"3":{"en":"5 cm"},"4":{"en":"10 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"252\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 252 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L126 26L226 159ZM126 109L126 159M132 159L132 153L126 153\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M126 26L126 159\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"109\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"109\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"176\" y=\"175\">6</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"82\">l = 10</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">r</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">h = 8</text></g></svg><br>Let \\(h = 2k\\), \\(a = 3k\\): \\(\\frac{1}{3}(9k^2)(2k) = 6k^3 = 384 \\Rightarrow k = 4\\)<br>So \\(h = 8\\), \\(a = 12\\), \\(l = \\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = 10\\)<br>\\(r = \\frac{\\frac{a}{2} \\cdot h}{\\frac{a}{2} + l} = \\frac{6 \\times 8}{6 + 10} = \\frac{48}{16}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"252\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 252 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L126 26L226 159ZM126 109L126 159M132 159L132 153L126 153\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M126 26L126 159\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"109\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"109\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"176\" y=\"175\">6</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"82\">l = 10</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">r</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">h = 8</text></g></svg><br>मान लीजिए \\(h = 2k\\), \\(a = 3k\\): \\(\\frac{1}{3}(9k^2)(2k) = 6k^3 = 384 \\Rightarrow k = 4\\)<br>अतः \\(h = 8\\), \\(a = 12\\), \\(l = \\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = 10\\)<br>\\(r = \\frac{\\frac{a}{2} \\cdot h}{\\frac{a}{2} + l} = \\frac{6 \\times 8}{6 + 10} = \\frac{48}{16}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072340","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has a square base of side s cm and height h cm. If the volume is 256 cm³ and height is double the side length, find s. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म का आधार वर्ग है जिसकी भुजा s cm और ऊँचाई h cm है। यदि आयतन 256 cm³ है और ऊँचाई भुजा की लंबाई की दोगुनी है, तो s ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(12\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{5}\\) cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"183\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"-27 0 183 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L95 186M26 186L26 48M95 186L129 164M95 186L95 48M26 48L95 48M26 48L60 26M129 164L129 26M95 48L129 26M60 26L129 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 186L60 164M60 164L129 164M60 164L60 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"60\" y=\"202\">s</text><text x=\"119\" y=\"190\">s</text><text x=\"-3\" y=\"121\">h = 2s</text></g></svg><br>\\(h = 2s\\), so \\(s^2 \\cdot 2s = 2s^3 = 256\\)<br>\\(s^3 = 128 = 64 \\times 2\\)<br>\\(s = \\boxed{4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"183\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"-27 0 183 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L95 186M26 186L26 48M95 186L129 164M95 186L95 48M26 48L95 48M26 48L60 26M129 164L129 26M95 48L129 26M60 26L129 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 186L60 164M60 164L129 164M60 164L60 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"60\" y=\"202\">s</text><text x=\"119\" y=\"190\">s</text><text x=\"-3\" y=\"121\">h = 2s</text></g></svg><br>\\(h = 2s\\), अतः \\(s^2 \\cdot 2s = 2s^3 = 256\\)<br>\\(s^3 = 128 = 64 \\times 2\\)<br>\\(s = \\boxed{4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072341","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"The length of the shadow of a tower is 9 m when the sun's altitude is 30°. What is the height of the tower? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जब सूर्य की ऊँचाई 30° है तब एक मीनार की छाया की लंबाई 9 m है। मीनार की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4½ m"},"2":{"en":"9√3 m"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"3√3 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L256 159M26 159L26 26M34 159L34 151L26 151M256 159L26 26M238 159A18 18 0 0 1 240 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"170\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"96\">h</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"256\" y=\"173\">C</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"175\">9 m (shadow)</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{9}\\)<br>\\(h = 9 \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = 3\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3√3 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L256 159M26 159L26 26M34 159L34 151L26 151M256 159L26 26M238 159A18 18 0 0 1 240 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"170\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"96\">h</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"256\" y=\"173\">C</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"175\">9 m (shadow)</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{9}\\)<br>\\(h = 9 \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = 3\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3√3 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072342","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Simplify (3x − 4y)² + (3x + 4y)². [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: (3x − 4y)² + (3x + 4y)²। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18x² + 16y²"},"2":{"en":"18x² − 32y²"},"3":{"en":"36x² + 32y²"},"4":{"en":"18x² + 32y²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((a-b)^2 + (a+b)^2 = 2(a^2 + b^2)\\)<br>\\(= 2(9x^2 + 16y^2)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{18x^2 + 32y^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 18x² + 32y².</b>","hi":"\\((a-b)^2 + (a+b)^2 = 2(a^2 + b^2)\\)<br>\\(= 2(9x^2 + 16y^2)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{18x^2 + 32y^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 18x² + 32y² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072343","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Simplify the expression (a + b)³ − (a − b)³. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"व्यंजक (a + b)³ − (a − b)³ को सरलीकृत कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6a²b + 2a³"},"2":{"en":"6ab² + 2a³"},"3":{"en":"2b³ + 6ab"},"4":{"en":"6a²b + 2b³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((a+b)^3 - (a-b)^3 = 2\\left[3a^2b + b^3\\right]\\)<br>\\(= 6a^2b + 2b^3\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6a^2b + 2b^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 6a²b + 2b³.</b>","hi":"\\((a+b)^3 - (a-b)^3 = 2\\left[3a^2b + b^3\\right]\\)<br>\\(= 6a^2b + 2b^3\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6a^2b + 2b^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 6a²b + 2b³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072344","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"For the equation 5x − 2y = 10, what is the slope of the line? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"समीकरण 5x − 2y = 10 के लिए, रेखा की प्रवणता क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5/3"},"2":{"en":"5/2"},"3":{"en":"3/2"},"4":{"en":"1/2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(2y = 5x - 10 \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{5}{2}x - 5\\)<br>Comparing with \\(y = mx + c\\)<br>\\(m = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 5/2.</b>","hi":"\\(2y = 5x - 10 \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{5}{2}x - 5\\)<br>\\(y = mx + c\\) से तुलना करने पर<br>\\(m = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 5/2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072345","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"The compound interest on a sum for 2 years at 12% per annum compounded annually is ₹2,544. What is the principal amount? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किसी धनराशि पर 12% प्रति वर्ष की दर से वार्षिक रूप से चक्रवृद्धि होने पर 2 वर्षों का चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज ₹2,544 है। मूलधन क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹10,000"},"2":{"en":"₹12,000"},"3":{"en":"₹13,000"},"4":{"en":"₹11,500"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Effective rate for 2 years \\(= 12 + 12 + \\frac{144}{100} = 25.44\\%\\)<br>\\(P \\times 0.2544 = 2544\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\boxed{10{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹10,000.</b>","hi":"2 वर्षों की प्रभावी दर \\(= 12 + 12 + \\frac{144}{100} = 25.44\\%\\)<br>\\(P \\times 0.2544 = 2544\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\boxed{10{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹10,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072346","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A Mumbai grocer has rice at ₹30/kg and ₹50/kg.<br>In what ratio should he mix them so that he can sell the mixture at ₹36/kg with no profit or loss? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मुंबई के एक व्यापारी के पास ₹30/kg और ₹50/kg के चावल हैं।<br>वह उन्हें किस अनुपात में मिलाए कि मिश्रण को ₹36/kg पर बिना लाभ या हानि के बेच सके? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4:1"},"2":{"en":"7:3"},"3":{"en":"6:1"},"4":{"en":"9:4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Alligation: cheaper : dearer \\(= (50 - 36) : (36 - 30)\\)<br>\\(= 14 : 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 7:3.</b>","hi":"मिश्रण नियम: सस्ता : महँगा \\(= (50 - 36) : (36 - 30)\\)<br>\\(= 14 : 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 7:3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072347","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"When comparing unemployment rates across five states using a bar diagram, what is important to maintain for accuracy? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बार आरेख का उपयोग करके पाँच राज्यों की बेरोज़गारी दरों की तुलना करते समय सटीकता के लिए क्या बनाए रखना महत्वपूर्ण है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Different scales for clarity","hi":"स्पष्टता के लिए अलग-अलग पैमाने"},"2":{"en":"Varying bar widths","hi":"बदलती बार चौड़ाई"},"3":{"en":"Same scale on the y-axis and equal bar width","hi":"y-अक्ष पर समान पैमाना और समान बार चौड़ाई"},"4":{"en":"Use different bar colours only","hi":"केवल अलग-अलग बार रंगों का उपयोग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"For a fair comparison, all bars must start from the same baseline and use one common scale<br>Equal bar width keeps the areas comparable, so only the heights convey the data<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Same scale on the y-axis and equal bar width}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Same scale on the y-axis and equal bar width.</b>","hi":"उचित तुलना के लिए सभी बार एक ही आधार रेखा से शुरू होने चाहिए और एक ही पैमाना प्रयोग होना चाहिए<br>समान बार चौड़ाई क्षेत्रफलों को तुलनीय रखती है, अतः केवल ऊँचाई डेटा दर्शाती है<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{y-अक्ष पर समान पैमाना और समान बार चौड़ाई}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): y-अक्ष पर समान पैमाना और समान बार चौड़ाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072348","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"In a histogram, what does the height of each bar represent? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक आयतचित्र में, प्रत्येक बार की ऊँचाई क्या दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Class width","hi":"वर्ग चौड़ाई"},"2":{"en":"Frequency density","hi":"आवृत्ति घनत्व"},"3":{"en":"Class midpoint","hi":"वर्ग मध्यबिंदु"},"4":{"en":"None of these","hi":"इनमें से कोई नहीं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A histogram plots frequency density against class intervals<br>The height of each bar is the frequency density \\(= \\frac{\\text{frequency}}{\\text{class width}}\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Frequency density}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Frequency density.</b>","hi":"आयतचित्र वर्ग अंतरालों के सापेक्ष आवृत्ति घनत्व दर्शाता है<br>प्रत्येक बार की ऊँचाई आवृत्ति घनत्व \\(= \\frac{\\text{आवृत्ति}}{\\text{वर्ग चौड़ाई}}\\) है<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{आवृत्ति घनत्व}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): आवृत्ति घनत्व है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072349","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosθ = 0, then sin²θ = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि cosθ = 0 है, तो sin²θ = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1\\)<br>With \\(\\cos\\theta = 0\\): \\(\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - 0\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2\\theta = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1\\)<br>\\(\\cos\\theta = 0\\) रखने पर: \\(\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - 0\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2\\theta = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072350","section":"MATH","topic":"Problems on Trains","question":{"en":"If a train takes 20 seconds to cross a platform of 180 m and the train's length is 120 m, what is its speed? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि कोई रेलगाड़ी 180 m के प्लेटफॉर्म को पार करने में 20 सेकंड लेती है और रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई 120 m है, तो उसकी गति क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45 km/h"},"2":{"en":"50 km/h"},"3":{"en":"60 km/h"},"4":{"en":"54 km/h"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Total distance \\(= 180 + 120 = 300\\) m<br>Speed \\(= \\frac{300}{20} = 15\\) m/s<br>\\(= 15 \\times \\frac{18}{5} = \\boxed{54\\ \\text{km/h}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 54 km/h.</b>","hi":"कुल दूरी \\(= 180 + 120 = 300\\) m<br>गति \\(= \\frac{300}{20} = 15\\) m/s<br>\\(= 15 \\times \\frac{18}{5} = \\boxed{54\\ \\text{km/h}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 54 km/h है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072351","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A can complete a work in 10 days and B in 15 days.<br>How long will it take them to finish the work if they work together? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"A किसी कार्य को 10 दिनों में और B 15 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है।<br>यदि वे साथ मिलकर कार्य करें तो उन्हें कार्य पूरा करने में कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 days","hi":"6 दिन"},"2":{"en":"7 days","hi":"7 दिन"},"3":{"en":"8 days","hi":"8 दिन"},"4":{"en":"9 days","hi":"9 दिन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Combined rate \\(= \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} = \\frac{3 + 2}{30} = \\frac{1}{6}\\)<br>Time \\(= \\boxed{6\\ \\text{days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 6 days.</b>","hi":"संयुक्त दर \\(= \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} = \\frac{3 + 2}{30} = \\frac{1}{6}\\)<br>समय \\(= \\boxed{6\\ \\text{दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 6 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072352","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circular pavilion, a support beam acts as a chord connecting two columns. The chord is 20 m, and the height from the chord to the top of the arc is 5 m. Find the radius of the circular roof. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्ताकार मंडप में, एक सहारा बीम दो स्तंभों को जोड़ने वाली जीवा के रूप में कार्य करता है। जीवा 20 m है और जीवा से चाप के शीर्ष तक की ऊँचाई 5 m है। वृत्ताकार छत की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13 m"},"2":{"en":"14 m"},"3":{"en":"12.5 m"},"4":{"en":"16 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 170L188 170M116 116L116 170M123 170L123 163L116 163\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 116L188 170M116 170L116 206\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"110\">O</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">r − 5</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"11\">10</text><text x=\"147\" y=\"154\">r</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">5</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{c}{2}\\right)^2 + h^2}{2h}\\) with \\(c = 20\\), \\(h = 5\\)<br>\\(r = \\frac{100 + 25}{10}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{12.5\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12.5 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 170L188 170M116 116L116 170M123 170L123 163L116 163\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 116L188 170M116 170L116 206\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"110\">O</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">r − 5</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"11\">10</text><text x=\"147\" y=\"154\">r</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">5</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{c}{2}\\right)^2 + h^2}{2h}\\), जहाँ \\(c = 20\\), \\(h = 5\\)<br>\\(r = \\frac{100 + 25}{10}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{12.5\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12.5 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072353","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A projectile launch angle satisfies sine twice the angle is 0.8 and cosine twice the angle is 0.6. Calculate sum of fourth powers of sine and cosine of the launch angle to predict range stability. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक प्रक्षेप्य के प्रक्षेपण कोण के लिए दुगुने कोण की ज्या 0.8 और दुगुने कोण की कोज्या 0.6 है। परास की स्थिरता का अनुमान लगाने के लिए प्रक्षेपण कोण की ज्या और कोज्या के चतुर्थ घातों का योग ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0.6"},"3":{"en":"0.68"},"4":{"en":"0.72"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin 2\\theta = 0.8 \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = 0.4\\)<br>\\(\\sin^4\\theta + \\cos^4\\theta = 1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - 2(0.16)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.68}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 0.68.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin 2\\theta = 0.8 \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = 0.4\\)<br>\\(\\sin^4\\theta + \\cos^4\\theta = 1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - 2(0.16)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.68}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 0.68 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072354","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In an optical system, two light beams hit a lens at angles x and y. The system's calibration requires finding the product of the sums of sine and cosine of these angles to optimize the focus. The engineers know that the difference of squares of their sine values is 1/4, and the difference of their sine and cosine products is 0.<br>Given: sin²x − sin²y = 1/4<br>sin x cos x − sin y cos y = 0<br>Find the value of (sin x + cos x) × (sin y + cos y). [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक प्रकाशिक तंत्र में, दो प्रकाश पुंज क्रमशः x और y कोणों पर लेंस पर पड़ते हैं। तंत्र के अंशांकन के लिए इन कोणों की ज्या और कोज्या के योगों का गुणनफल ज्ञात करना आवश्यक है। अभियंताओं को ज्ञात है कि इनकी ज्या मानों के वर्गों का अंतर 1/4 है और उनके ज्या-कोज्या गुणनफलों का अंतर 0 है।<br>दिया गया है: sin²x − sin²y = 1/4<br>sin x cos x − sin y cos y = 0<br>(sin x + cos x) × (sin y + cos y) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.5"},"2":{"en":"1.775"},"3":{"en":"1.968"},"4":{"en":"2.25"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin x\\cos x = \\sin y\\cos y \\Rightarrow \\sin 2x = \\sin 2y\\), so \\(x + y = 90°\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2x - \\sin^2y = \\sin(x+y)\\sin(x-y) = \\sin(x-y) = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(\\sin 2x = \\cos(x - y) = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{1}{16}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4} = 0.968\\)<br>\\((\\sin x + \\cos x)(\\sin y + \\cos y) = \\sqrt{(1 + \\sin 2x)(1 + \\sin 2y)} = 1 + \\sin 2x\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1.968}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.968.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin x\\cos x = \\sin y\\cos y \\Rightarrow \\sin 2x = \\sin 2y\\), अतः \\(x + y = 90°\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2x - \\sin^2y = \\sin(x+y)\\sin(x-y) = \\sin(x-y) = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(\\sin 2x = \\cos(x - y) = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{1}{16}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4} = 0.968\\)<br>\\((\\sin x + \\cos x)(\\sin y + \\cos y) = \\sqrt{(1 + \\sin 2x)(1 + \\sin 2y)} = 1 + \\sin 2x\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1.968}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1.968 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072355","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"This histogram represents the weights (in kg) of 45 people in a fitness club.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Which weight interval represents approximately one-fourth of the total people? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यह आयतचित्र एक फिटनेस क्लब के 45 व्यक्तियों के भार (kg में) को दर्शाता है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>कौन-सा भार अंतराल कुल व्यक्तियों का लगभग एक-चौथाई दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40-45 kg"},"2":{"en":"50-55 kg"},"3":{"en":"55-60 kg"},"4":{"en":"60-65 kg"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Total people \\(= 45\\), so one-fourth \\(\\approx 11.25\\)<br>Reading the bars: 40–45 → 5, 45–50 → 8, 50–55 → 12, 55–60 → 10, 60–65 → 7, 65–70 → 3<br>The interval closest to 11.25 is 50–55 with 12 people<br>\\(\\boxed{50-55\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 50-55 kg.</b>","hi":"कुल व्यक्ति \\(= 45\\), अतः एक-चौथाई \\(\\approx 11.25\\)<br>बार पढ़ने पर: 40–45 → 5, 45–50 → 8, 50–55 → 12, 55–60 → 10, 60–65 → 7, 65–70 → 3<br>11.25 के निकटतम अंतराल 50–55 है जिसमें 12 व्यक्ति हैं<br>\\(\\boxed{50-55\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 50-55 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg"]}}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072356","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word<b>. Enigmatic</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Obscure"},"2":{"en":"Lucid"},"3":{"en":"Arcane"},"4":{"en":"Ambiguous"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Enigmatic (रहस्यमय) = difficult to interpret or understand; mysterious.</b><br><b>Lucid (स्पष्ट)</b> = clear and easy to understand ✔<br><b>Obscure (अस्पष्ट)</b> – synonym<br><b>Arcane (गूढ़)</b> – synonym<br><b>Ambiguous (द्व्यर्थक, अस्पष्ट)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: clear, transparent, plain.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Lucid.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072357","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the sentence containing the homonym of the underlined word:</b><br>The <u>match</u> was very exciting. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He used a match to light the candle."},"2":{"en":"The match was watched by millions."},"3":{"en":"That match ended in a draw."},"4":{"en":"Football matches are thrilling."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Match (मुकाबला / माचिस की तीली) – a homonym: same spelling, different meanings.</b><br>In the given sentence, 'match' means a sports contest.<br>Option 1 uses 'match' as a small stick that produces fire – a different meaning, so it is the homonym.<br>Options 2, 3 and 4 all use 'match' in the same sense of a game or contest.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): He used a match to light the candle.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072358","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given direct speech into indirect speech appropriately.<br>She said, \"I need some rest now\". [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said that she needs some rest now"},"2":{"en":"She said that she is needing some rest now"},"3":{"en":"She said that she needed some rest then"},"4":{"en":"She said that she needs some rest then"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past reporting verb → simple present becomes simple past; 'now' becomes 'then'; 'I' → 'she'.</b><br>Indirect: She said that she <b>needed</b> some rest <b>then</b>.<br>Option 1 – tense and 'now' not changed<br>Option 2 – 'is needing' is wrong (stative verb) and 'now' not changed<br>Option 4 – tense not changed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She said that she needed some rest then.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072359","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given indirect speech into direct speech appropriately:<br><br>She said that she had completed the task. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said, \"I completes the task\"."},"2":{"en":"She said, \"I completed the task\"."},"3":{"en":"She said, \"I would have completed the task\"."},"4":{"en":"She said, \"I will complete the task\"."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: In direct speech the past perfect of reported speech goes back to the simple past (or present perfect); 'she' → 'I'.</b><br>Direct: She said, \"I <b>completed</b> the task\".<br>Option 1 – 'I completes' breaks subject-verb agreement<br>Option 3 – conditional 'would have completed' changes the meaning<br>Option 4 – future tense changes the meaning<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She said, \"I completed the task\".</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072360","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br><br>A) affordable medicines<br>B) through Jan Aushadhi Kendras<br>C) are being made available<br>D) to the public [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D-B-C-A"},"2":{"en":"B-A-D-C"},"3":{"en":"A-D-C-B"},"4":{"en":"A-C-D-B"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: A-C-D-B</b><br><b>A</b> 'affordable medicines' is the subject.<br><b>C</b> 'are being made available' is the verb.<br><b>D</b> 'to the public' tells to whom.<br><b>B</b> 'through Jan Aushadhi Kendras' tells by what means.<br>Affordable medicines are being made available to the public through Jan Aushadhi Kendras.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): A-C-D-B.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072361","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the <b>spelling error</b>: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Irrefutable"},"2":{"en":"Hieroglyphics"},"3":{"en":"Anomally"},"4":{"en":"Euphemism"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Anomaly (विसंगति) = something that differs from what is normal.</b><br><b>Anomally</b> is misspelt – it has a single 'l'.<br><b>Irrefutable (अकाट्य)</b> = impossible to disprove – correct<br><b>Hieroglyphics (चित्रलिपि)</b> = picture writing of ancient Egypt – correct<br><b>Euphemism (सौम्योक्ति)</b> = a mild word used for a harsh one – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Anomally.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072362","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correct degree of comparison:<br><br>India is one of the _________ growing economies in the world, attracting significant foreign investments. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"more fast"},"2":{"en":"most fast"},"3":{"en":"faster"},"4":{"en":"fastest"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'one of the' is followed by the superlative degree + plural noun.</b><br>'fast' is a one-syllable adjective, so its superlative is 'fastest'.<br>Correct sentence: India is one of the <b>fastest</b> growing economies in the world…<br>more fast – wrong comparative form<br>most fast – 'most' is not used with one-syllable adjectives<br>faster – comparative cannot follow 'one of the'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): fastest.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072363","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Identify the option that best corrects the highlighted part of the sentence for proper grammar and usage.<br><br>He prevented me to go outside. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"from going outside"},"2":{"en":"with going outside"},"3":{"en":"for going outside"},"4":{"en":"by going outside"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'prevent someone from + V-ing' is the correct pattern.</b><br>'prevent … to go' is wrong.<br>Correct sentence: He prevented me <b>from going</b> outside.<br>with, for, by – none is used with 'prevent' in this sense<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): from going outside.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072364","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Identify the option that best corrects the highlighted part of the sentence for proper grammar and usage.<br><br>He is angry on his friend for the mistake. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"angry for"},"2":{"en":"angry with"},"3":{"en":"angry in"},"4":{"en":"angry by"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'angry with' a person; 'angry at/about' a thing.</b><br>'his friend' is a person, so 'angry with'.<br>Correct sentence: He is <b>angry with</b> his friend for the mistake.<br>angry for, angry in, angry by – incorrect prepositions with 'angry'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): angry with.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072365","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Spot the error in the following sentence and identify the INCORRECT part.<br><br>He has been afraid from spiders since childhood. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"afraid from"},"2":{"en":"spiders"},"3":{"en":"since childhood"},"4":{"en":"No error"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The adjective 'afraid' takes the preposition 'of'.</b><br>'afraid from' is wrong.<br>Correct sentence: He has been <b>afraid of</b> spiders since childhood.<br>'spiders' – correct plural noun<br>'since childhood' – 'since' correctly marks a point of time with the present perfect<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): afraid from.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072366","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Spot the error in the following sentence and identify the INCORRECT part.<br><br>She always avoids to speak during the meetings because she is shy. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"always avoids"},"2":{"en":"to speak"},"3":{"en":"during the meetings"},"4":{"en":"No error"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'avoid' is followed by a gerund (V-ing), not a to-infinitive.</b><br>'avoids to speak' must be 'avoids speaking'.<br>Correct sentence: She always avoids <b>speaking</b> during the meetings because she is shy.<br>'always avoids' – correct verb with singular subject<br>'during the meetings' – correct preposition<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): to speak.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072367","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"There are four jumbled sentences given below.<br><br>Your task is to rearrange them into a logically coherent and meaningful paragraph and choose the correct sequence from the given options.<br><br>1. Students are encouraged to work on real-life problem-solving.<br>2. The Atal Innovation Mission promotes start-up culture in schools and colleges.<br>3. It provides funding and mentoring for innovation labs.<br>4. This has led to student-led projects in rural technology and healthcare. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"3":{"en":"2-3-1-4"},"4":{"en":"1-3-4-2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-3-1-4</b><br><b>2</b> introduces the subject: the Atal Innovation Mission.<br><b>3</b> 'It provides…' – 'It' refers to the Mission.<br><b>1</b> explains what students do in these labs.<br><b>4</b> 'This has led to…' gives the result.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2-3-1-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072368","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"What is the antonym of the word \"sophisticated\"? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Controlled"},"2":{"en":"Cultured"},"3":{"en":"Refined"},"4":{"en":"Simple"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Sophisticated (परिष्कृत, जटिल) = highly developed and complex; worldly and refined.</b><br><b>Simple (सरल)</b> = plain, not complex ✔<br><b>Controlled (नियंत्रित)</b> – unrelated<br><b>Cultured (सुसंस्कृत)</b> – synonym<br><b>Refined (परिष्कृत)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: naive, unrefined, crude.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Simple.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072369","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below :<br><b>“Bury the hatchet”</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hide evidence of wrongdoing"},"2":{"en":"Bury something literally"},"3":{"en":"End a conflict and make peace"},"4":{"en":"Start a new quarrel"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Bury the hatchet (बैर भुलाना, सुलह करना) = to end a quarrel and become friendly again.</b><br>Example: After years of rivalry, the two leaders buried the hatchet.<br>Hide evidence (सबूत छिपाना) – unrelated<br>Bury something literally (शाब्दिक रूप से गाड़ना) – literal reading<br>Start a new quarrel (नया झगड़ा) – opposite<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): End a conflict and make peace.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072370","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br><b>“Go the whole hog”</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Refuse to try"},"2":{"en":"Do something completely"},"3":{"en":"Be lazy"},"4":{"en":"Plan early"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Go the whole hog (पूरी तरह करना) = to do something thoroughly and completely.</b><br>Example: They went the whole hog and renovated the entire house.<br>Refuse to try (कोशिश न करना) – opposite<br>Be lazy (आलसी होना) – opposite<br>Plan early (पहले योजना बनाना) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Do something completely.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072371","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the appropriate one-word substitution for:<br><br>A person who composes music. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vocalist"},"2":{"en":"Singer"},"3":{"en":"Lyricist"},"4":{"en":"Composer"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Composer (संगीतकार) = a person who writes music.</b><br><b>Vocalist (गायक)</b> = a person who sings, especially in a band<br><b>Singer (गायक)</b> = a person who sings<br><b>Lyricist (गीतकार)</b> = a person who writes the words of songs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Composer.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072372","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.</b><br>1. Final version was published online.<br>2. Experts were consulted for feedback.<br>3. A preliminary draft was circulated.<br>4. Comments were incorporated and edits were made. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-2-3-4"},"2":{"en":"4-1-2-3"},"3":{"en":"4-2-1-3"},"4":{"en":"3-2-4-1"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 3-2-4-1</b><br><b>3</b> The process begins with a preliminary draft.<br><b>2</b> Experts give feedback on the draft.<br><b>4</b> Their comments are incorporated.<br><b>1</b> The final version is published – the last step.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3-2-4-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072373","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence</b><br><b>P.</b> as part of a nationwide public health intervention <b>Q.</b> through mobile diagnostic units <b>R.</b> regular screening camps <b>S.</b> were conducted in remote and underserved areas [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RQSP"},"2":{"en":"RSPQ"},"3":{"en":"QPRS"},"4":{"en":"PRSQ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RSPQ</b><br><b>R</b> 'regular screening camps' is the subject.<br><b>S</b> 'were conducted in remote and underserved areas' gives the verb and place.<br><b>P</b> 'as part of a nationwide public health intervention' gives the purpose.<br><b>Q</b> 'through mobile diagnostic units' closes with the means.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RSPQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072374","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence</b><br><b>P.</b> by integrating machine learning diagnostics <b>Q.</b> to minimize false negatives <b>R.</b> the AI-powered screening tool <b>S.</b> has significantly improved early disease detection [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RSPQ"},"2":{"en":"RQPS"},"3":{"en":"PQRS"},"4":{"en":"RPSQ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RSPQ</b><br><b>R</b> 'the AI-powered screening tool' is the subject.<br><b>S</b> 'has significantly improved early disease detection' gives the verb.<br><b>P</b> 'by integrating machine learning diagnostics' tells how.<br><b>Q</b> 'to minimize false negatives' gives the purpose of the diagnostics.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RSPQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072375","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence</b><br><b>P.</b> reflecting the precarious balance between economic development and environmental conservation <b>Q.</b> the recent Supreme Court judgment on mining activities in forest regions <b>R.</b> has set a legal precedent <b>S.</b> for all future industrial clearance protocols [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPRS"},"2":{"en":"QRSP"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"QSRP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br><b>Q</b> 'the recent Supreme Court judgment…' is the subject.<br><b>R</b> 'has set a legal precedent' gives the verb.<br><b>S</b> 'for all future industrial clearance protocols' completes the precedent.<br><b>P</b> 'reflecting the precarious balance…' adds a participle phrase at the end.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072376","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.</b><br>The domain of outer space, once a sublime expanse emblematic of universal aspiration, has morphed into a <b>(1)</b>____ terrain, rife with techno-nationalistic rivalries and juridical lacunae. As states and non-state actors alike pursue orbital hegemony, the narrative has shifted from exploration to securitization. The proliferation of constellations, kinetic kill vehicles, and cyber-vulnerable architectures has <b>(2)</b>____ erstwhile doctrinal separations between civilian and military enterprises. Multilateral compacts, such as the Outer Space Treaty, now appear <b>(3)</b>____ in the face of unilateral adventurism and semantic exploitation of treaty ambiguities. The ethos of cooperative multilateralism is steadily eclipsed by strategic opacity and regime fragmentation. Resource extraction from asteroids and prospective Mars colonization introduce a lexicon of planetary commodification, propelling a new phase of <b>(4)</b>____ governance, where legitimacy is brokered not by consensus but by technological primacy. Increasingly, legal constructs are subordinated to hardware capability, and soft power is reconstituted through launch cadence, orbital coverage, and downstream data monopolies. In this milieu, techno-diplomacy must evolve beyond hortatory platitudes to a <b>(5)</b>____ apparatus for strategic calibration, deterrence, and geopolitical signaling in an emergent multipolar cosmodynamic order.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 1? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"sanctified"},"2":{"en":"labyrinthine"},"3":{"en":"terrestrial"},"4":{"en":"homogenized"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…has morphed into a (1)____ terrain, rife with techno-nationalistic rivalries and juridical lacunae.\"</i><br>A terrain full of rivalries and legal gaps is complicated and confusing.<br><b>Labyrinthine (भूलभुलैया जैसा, जटिल)</b> ✔<br><b>Sanctified (पवित्र किया गया)</b> – opposite of 'rife with rivalries'<br><b>Terrestrial (स्थलीय)</b> – of the earth; space is not terrestrial<br><b>Homogenized (एकरूप किया गया)</b> – uniform; contradicts the rivalries<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): labyrinthine.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072377","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.</b><br>The domain of outer space, once a sublime expanse emblematic of universal aspiration, has morphed into a <b>(1)</b>____ terrain, rife with techno-nationalistic rivalries and juridical lacunae. As states and non-state actors alike pursue orbital hegemony, the narrative has shifted from exploration to securitization. The proliferation of constellations, kinetic kill vehicles, and cyber-vulnerable architectures has <b>(2)</b>____ erstwhile doctrinal separations between civilian and military enterprises. Multilateral compacts, such as the Outer Space Treaty, now appear <b>(3)</b>____ in the face of unilateral adventurism and semantic exploitation of treaty ambiguities. The ethos of cooperative multilateralism is steadily eclipsed by strategic opacity and regime fragmentation. Resource extraction from asteroids and prospective Mars colonization introduce a lexicon of planetary commodification, propelling a new phase of <b>(4)</b>____ governance, where legitimacy is brokered not by consensus but by technological primacy. Increasingly, legal constructs are subordinated to hardware capability, and soft power is reconstituted through launch cadence, orbital coverage, and downstream data monopolies. In this milieu, techno-diplomacy must evolve beyond hortatory platitudes to a <b>(5)</b>____ apparatus for strategic calibration, deterrence, and geopolitical signaling in an emergent multipolar cosmodynamic order.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 2? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"elided"},"2":{"en":"accentuated"},"3":{"en":"punctuated"},"4":{"en":"amalgamated"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"The proliferation of constellations, kinetic kill vehicles… has (2)____ erstwhile doctrinal separations between civilian and military enterprises.\"</i><br>Dual-use space technology has removed the old line between civilian and military uses.<br><b>Elided (मिटा दिया, लुप्त कर दिया)</b> = removed or blurred ✔<br><b>Accentuated (उभारा)</b> – would sharpen the separation; opposite<br><b>Punctuated (बीच-बीच में बाधित किया)</b> – does not fit 'separations'<br><b>Amalgamated (मिला दिया)</b> – used for joining things, not for removing a separation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): elided.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072378","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.</b><br>The domain of outer space, once a sublime expanse emblematic of universal aspiration, has morphed into a <b>(1)</b>____ terrain, rife with techno-nationalistic rivalries and juridical lacunae. As states and non-state actors alike pursue orbital hegemony, the narrative has shifted from exploration to securitization. The proliferation of constellations, kinetic kill vehicles, and cyber-vulnerable architectures has <b>(2)</b>____ erstwhile doctrinal separations between civilian and military enterprises. Multilateral compacts, such as the Outer Space Treaty, now appear <b>(3)</b>____ in the face of unilateral adventurism and semantic exploitation of treaty ambiguities. The ethos of cooperative multilateralism is steadily eclipsed by strategic opacity and regime fragmentation. Resource extraction from asteroids and prospective Mars colonization introduce a lexicon of planetary commodification, propelling a new phase of <b>(4)</b>____ governance, where legitimacy is brokered not by consensus but by technological primacy. Increasingly, legal constructs are subordinated to hardware capability, and soft power is reconstituted through launch cadence, orbital coverage, and downstream data monopolies. In this milieu, techno-diplomacy must evolve beyond hortatory platitudes to a <b>(5)</b>____ apparatus for strategic calibration, deterrence, and geopolitical signaling in an emergent multipolar cosmodynamic order.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 3? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"inviolate"},"2":{"en":"vestigial"},"3":{"en":"implacable"},"4":{"en":"fungible"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Multilateral compacts, such as the Outer Space Treaty, now appear (3)____ in the face of unilateral adventurism…\"</i><br>Old treaties seem weak and outdated before new unilateral actions.<br><b>Vestigial (अवशेषी, निष्प्रभावी)</b> = remaining but no longer useful ✔<br><b>Inviolate (अखंड)</b> – unbroken; opposite<br><b>Implacable (अटल)</b> – unstoppable; opposite of weak<br><b>Fungible (परस्पर विनिमेय)</b> – interchangeable; unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): vestigial.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072379","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.</b><br>The domain of outer space, once a sublime expanse emblematic of universal aspiration, has morphed into a <b>(1)</b>____ terrain, rife with techno-nationalistic rivalries and juridical lacunae. As states and non-state actors alike pursue orbital hegemony, the narrative has shifted from exploration to securitization. The proliferation of constellations, kinetic kill vehicles, and cyber-vulnerable architectures has <b>(2)</b>____ erstwhile doctrinal separations between civilian and military enterprises. Multilateral compacts, such as the Outer Space Treaty, now appear <b>(3)</b>____ in the face of unilateral adventurism and semantic exploitation of treaty ambiguities. The ethos of cooperative multilateralism is steadily eclipsed by strategic opacity and regime fragmentation. Resource extraction from asteroids and prospective Mars colonization introduce a lexicon of planetary commodification, propelling a new phase of <b>(4)</b>____ governance, where legitimacy is brokered not by consensus but by technological primacy. Increasingly, legal constructs are subordinated to hardware capability, and soft power is reconstituted through launch cadence, orbital coverage, and downstream data monopolies. In this milieu, techno-diplomacy must evolve beyond hortatory platitudes to a <b>(5)</b>____ apparatus for strategic calibration, deterrence, and geopolitical signaling in an emergent multipolar cosmodynamic order.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 4? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"extractivist"},"2":{"en":"fiduciary"},"3":{"en":"anachronistic"},"4":{"en":"restitutive"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Resource extraction from asteroids… introduce a lexicon of planetary commodification, propelling a new phase of (4)____ governance…\"</i><br>Governance driven by resource extraction is extractivist.<br><b>Extractivist (संसाधन-दोहन आधारित)</b> ✔<br><b>Fiduciary (न्यासी)</b> – based on trust; unrelated<br><b>Anachronistic (कालभ्रमित)</b> – out of date; the phase is new<br><b>Restitutive (क्षतिपूर्ति संबंधी)</b> – about restoring loss; unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): extractivist.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072380","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.</b><br>The domain of outer space, once a sublime expanse emblematic of universal aspiration, has morphed into a <b>(1)</b>____ terrain, rife with techno-nationalistic rivalries and juridical lacunae. As states and non-state actors alike pursue orbital hegemony, the narrative has shifted from exploration to securitization. The proliferation of constellations, kinetic kill vehicles, and cyber-vulnerable architectures has <b>(2)</b>____ erstwhile doctrinal separations between civilian and military enterprises. Multilateral compacts, such as the Outer Space Treaty, now appear <b>(3)</b>____ in the face of unilateral adventurism and semantic exploitation of treaty ambiguities. The ethos of cooperative multilateralism is steadily eclipsed by strategic opacity and regime fragmentation. Resource extraction from asteroids and prospective Mars colonization introduce a lexicon of planetary commodification, propelling a new phase of <b>(4)</b>____ governance, where legitimacy is brokered not by consensus but by technological primacy. Increasingly, legal constructs are subordinated to hardware capability, and soft power is reconstituted through launch cadence, orbital coverage, and downstream data monopolies. In this milieu, techno-diplomacy must evolve beyond hortatory platitudes to a <b>(5)</b>____ apparatus for strategic calibration, deterrence, and geopolitical signaling in an emergent multipolar cosmodynamic order.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 5? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"palliative"},"2":{"en":"perfunctory"},"3":{"en":"prophylactic"},"4":{"en":"prosaic"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…techno-diplomacy must evolve beyond hortatory platitudes to a (5)____ apparatus for strategic calibration, deterrence…\"</i><br>Deterrence aims to prevent conflict before it happens.<br><b>Prophylactic (निवारक)</b> = preventive ✔<br><b>Palliative (उपशामक)</b> – relieves symptoms without removing the cause<br><b>Perfunctory (दिखावटी, औपचारिक)</b> – done without care; opposite of 'evolve beyond platitudes'<br><b>Prosaic (नीरस, साधारण)</b> – ordinary; does not fit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): prophylactic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};